  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/84759361307833173623">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated March 30, 2009
A controversial rock star of professional hockey - with a taste for high fashion and a reputation for violent outbursts - Sean Avery has returned to his role as the New York Rangers' agitator extraordinaire.
Born in Pickering, Ontario, Mr. Avery, a forward, broke into the N.H.L. at 20, joining the Detroit Red Wings in 2000. Mr. Avery was traded to the Rangers from the Los Angeles Kings in February 2007, playing 86 games over two seasons with the team before signing a four-year, $15.5 million contract with the Dallas Stars in July 2008 as an unrestricted free agent. In March 2009, the Rangers brought back Mr. Avery after he was waived by the Dallas team following a league suspension.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">1</nyt:number_of_variants>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/a/sean_avery/index.html"/>
