    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-12-02</nyt:latest_use>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated Dec. 2, 2009
By William J. Broad
Mohamed ElBaradei, an Egyptian-born lawyer and Nobel Peace Prize winner, headed the International Atomic Energy Agency for 12 years. He gained attention when he became the West's main way of negotiating with Iran over its nuclear program. His star rose as European diplomacy stalled and as American credibility on atomic intelligence declined.
Dr. ElBaradiei was succeeded by Yukiya Amano on Dec. 1, 2009.
In an interview, Dr. ElBaradei called the global system for nuclear security "a mess," saying events were undermining authorities and promoting crises and dangerous proliferation trends.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/e/mohamed_elbaradei/index.html"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
