  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/N86794285690561607873">
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-06-14</nyt:latest_use>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Holyfield, Evander</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">At 46, Evander Holyfield believed that he had one good bout left, maybe more, in his still sculptured body. He unsuccessfully tried to summon it Dec. 20, 2008, in Zurich in a match with Nikolai Valuev, a 7-foot Russian. At stake was the World Boxing Association heavyweight belt. Holyfield wanted to buckle it around a waist that has barely expanded since he won his first professional title in 1990. The match may have been Holyfield’s last chance at winning a fifth heavyweight title. He had hoped to surpass George Foreman, who did it against Michael Moorer at age 45 in 1994.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2004-11-14</nyt:first_use>
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">1</nyt:number_of_variants>
