    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated June 19, 2009
Rafael Nadal is the number one ranked tennis player in the world. At 23, Nada, a Spaniard from Manacor on the island of Mallorca, has won six Grand Slam singles titles, including four French Open championships, and an Olympic Gold Medal in the 2008 games in Beijing. He is strong on all surfaces, but particularly hard to beat on clay.
Tennis fans were disappointed when Nadal, nicknamed "Rafa," announced that he would not play Wimbledon in 2009 because of tendinitis in his knees. He would have been the top-seeded player and a favorite for the championship along with Roger Federer.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:associated_article_count rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">181</nyt:associated_article_count>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Nadal, Rafael</skos:prefLabel>
  </rdf:Description>
