  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/84759508104656122903">
    <nyt:associated_article_count rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">2</nyt:associated_article_count>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/c/susan_cheever/index.html"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Susan Cheever is a novelist, a biographer and the only daughter of the late writer John Cheever. Her latest book, her 13th, is ?Desire: Where Sex Meets Addiction,? a cautionary tome about what she calls her sexual addiction.
She grew up in literary New York, but it was not entirely a privileged upbringing, as she told in ?Home Before Dark,? her well-received if controversial 1984 biography of her father. An alcoholic and a philanderer, Mr. Cheever was tormented by his bisexuality. He also made no secret of his disappointment in the adolescent Susan?s looks, telling her to lose weight. (His journals revealed his fantasies that she would be a great beauty who would make a brilliant match, down to the conversations he would have with the wealthy father of the groom.)</skos:definition>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2008-11-16</nyt:latest_use>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/cheever_susan_per"/>
