  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/51636998897307375873">
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-06-05</nyt:latest_use>
    <nyt:associated_article_count rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">10</nyt:associated_article_count>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated June 4, 2009
Gianni Versace, the Italian fashion designer of ornately decorated and sometimes outrageously revealing gowns, was a driving force in the glamorizing of fashion during the era of supermodels and celebrity designers. He was shot to death, on July 15, 1997, outside his Miami home - the fifth victim of the suspected killer Andrew Cunanan, who committed suicide nine days later.
Amy M. Spindler, the former fashion critic of The New York Times and style editor of its magazine, wrote in an obituary: "It is difficult to imagine another designer whose death would drain more life from the industry, an industry now driven by contemporary culture because Mr. Versace made it that way."</skos:definition>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/versace_gianni_per"/>
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">1</nyt:number_of_variants>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
