    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Gotti, John A</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated Dec. 2, 2009
When his father was convicted of murder and racketeering in 1992 and sent to prison for life, John A. â€œJuniorâ€ Gotti became the acting head of the Gambino crime family. He did a lot of strutting, made a lot of money illicitly, then pleaded guilty to racketeering in 1999 and served several years in prison.
Since then he has escaped conviction on additional charges. A federal jury failed on Dec. 1, 2009, for the fourth time in four years to reach a verdict in the prosecution of Mr. Gotti, enshrining him as a legendary criminal defendant and a mobster even trickier to convict than his father, John J. Gotti, who avoided conviction three times before being found guilty and dying in a federal prison hospital 10 years later.</skos:definition>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.junior_gotti"/>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/g/john_a_gotti/index.html"/>
