    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated Dec. 14, 2009
has replaced Ms. Sawyer on the morning show. George Stephanopoulos Diane Sawyer is a broadcast journalist for ABC, and was the longtime host of â€œGood Morning Americaâ€ until Dec. 11, 2009. In September, ABC announced that Ms. Sawyer, 63, would become the anchor of â€œWorld News,â€ the networkâ€™s evening news program. She will start in December, replacing Charles Gibson, who is retiring.
With Ms. Sawyerâ€™s ascension to â€œWorld News,â€ two of the three network evening newscasts will be anchored by women. Katie Couric took over the â€œCBS Evening Newsâ€ in 2006.</skos:definition>
