  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/82463623177241359703">
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.joe_torre"/>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/t/joe_torre/index.html"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">As manager of the New York Yankees, Joe Torre led the team to four World Series titles and trips to the postseason in each of his 12 years in the job.
When Torre took the job with the Yankees shortly after the 1995 season, the longest tenure for a manager under George Steinbrenner, the teamâ€™s volatile owner, had been four seasons. The hire of Torre initially raised some skepticism among fans, some dubbing him â€œClueless Joe.â€ During his previous managerial stints, with the New York Mets, Atlanta Braves and St. Louis Cardinals, he had compiled a record of 894-1,003. Those hackles didnâ€™t make it through his first season with the Yankees, when the team came from behind to win their first World Series title in 18 years.</skos:definition>
