  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/48414760255347932773">
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.edvard_munch"/>
    <nyt:search_api_query rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://api.nytimes.com/svc/search/v1/article?query=+nytd_per_facet%3A%5BMunch%2C+Edvard%5D&amp;rank=newest&amp;fields=abstract,author,body,byline,classifiers_facet,column_facet,date,day_of_week_facet,des_facet,desk_facet,fee,geo_facet,lead_paragraph,material_type_facet,multimedia,nytd_byline,nytd_des_facet,nytd_geo_facet,nytd_lead_paragraph,nytd_org_facet,nytd_per_facet,nytd_section_facet,nytd_title,nytd_works_mentioned_facet,org_facet,page_facet,per_facet,publication_day,publication_month,publication_year,section_page_facet,small_image_height,small_image_url,small_image_width,source_facet,title,url,word_count,works_mentioned_facet</nyt:search_api_query>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated Feb. 12, 2009
Edvard Munch (1863-1944) is widely thought to have done his best work between 1892 and 1908, while he ricocheted restlessly among Norway, Paris and Berlin. During this time he absorbed the latest styles, like Impressionism, and contributed to the founding of some new ones, particularly French Symbolism and German Expressionism. All his best-known paintings were made during the early 1890's; his innovative woodcuts dated from the turn of the century.
Few careers have become so completely identified with a single, emblematic work as Munch's has with ''The Scream,'' a staple of coffee cups, T-shirts, cartoons and inflatable toys. Leonardo's ''Mona Lisa,'' Géricault's ''Raft of the Medusa,'' and Seurat's ''Sunday Afternoon on the Grande Jatte'' approach such one-to-one efficiency. But Munch's pale, wailing ghost face may have the edge: simple, built for graphic reproduction, it is an emblem of modern angst. Munch painted ''The Scream'' in 1893. Most people are astounded to learn that he lived and worked for 50 more years.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Munch, Edvard</skos:prefLabel>
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">2</nyt:number_of_variants>
