    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Thurber, James</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.james_thurber"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">James Thurber, author, humorist and New York cartoonist, will be best remember for his hilarious tales, his indescribable dogs and his unforgettable character, Walter Mitty.
His tales were mingles with the exploits of unicorns, enraged wives, stupid athletes and excitable relatives. His drawings of dogs, which he produced with abundance on the backs of envelopes, in telephone books and on tablecloths, had a quality that seemed to link them with no other beast on Earth.
E.B. White, a New Yorker colleague of Mr. Thurber, wrote of him:</skos:definition>
    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2004-11-28</nyt:first_use>
