    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/p/peter_g_peterson/index.html"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Peter G. Peterson is one of a growing number of philanthropists whose foundations are spending increasing amounts and raising their voices to influence public policy ? a marked shift from their traditional position.
The Peter G. Peterson Foundation it is perhaps the only philanthropic organization seeking to address the issue of taxes, deficits and fiscal responsibility.
It is hard to mistake Mr. Peterson, a Wall Street billionaire and commerce secretary in the Nixon administration, for Michael Moore, the wise-cracking anti-establishment filmmaker. But Mr. Peterson has taken a page from Mr. Moore?s playbook, financing the documentary ?I.O.U.S.A.,? a searing look at the country?s addiction to debt.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Peterson, Peter G</skos:prefLabel>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.peter_george_peterson"/>
