    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: Aug. 7, 2009
.  National Endowment for the Humanities Jim Leach, a former Republican congressman from Iowa, is the new chairman of the 
During his 30 years in the House of Representatives, he founded and was co-chairman of the Congressional Humanities Caucus, which advocates in the House on behalf of the humanities and seeks to raise the profile of humanities nationwide. The endowment is a federal agency with a budget of $155 million that gives grants to support research, education, preservation and public programs in the humanities.
during the 1990s. National Endowment for the Arts  School of Public and International Affairs. At the time of his nomination, he said he felt comfortable serving a Democratic administration, despite being a Republican; he endorsed Mr. Obama in the 2008 election. "I think we have a unique, uplifting presidency," he said. Mr. Leach said he had started the humanities caucus partly to counteract the attacks against the National Endowment for the Humanities and the  Woodrow Wilson 's  Princeton University After leaving Congress, Mr. Leach became a professor at</skos:definition>
