  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/91214284054138217253">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Betty Currie, former personal secretary to President Bill Clinton, is the latest member of the Clinton administration to work for the Obama transition team. Ms. Currie, in a volunteer role, answers phones for the co-chairman of President-elect Barack Obama?s transition, John D. Podesta.
Ms. Currie, 69, who was caught up in an independent counsel investigation into Mr. Clinton's trysts with the White House intern Monica Lewinsky, has shied from publicity since retiring from her post. She lives in Hollywood, Md., with her husband, Bob, and Socks, the presidential cat, which she took with her after Mr. Clinton left office.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Currie, Betty</skos:prefLabel>
