    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: June 18, 2009
of Iran in a disputed presidential election. The announcement of Mr. Ahmadinejad's victory -- he was declared to have received more than 60 percent of the vote -- prompted intense protests by demonstrators who claimed that he had stolen the election. Mahmoud Ahmadinejad On June 13, 2009, Mir Hussein Moussavi was defeated by President
Mr. Moussavi, a former prime minister with a reputation for honesty and competence, rejected the results and called on supporters and clerics to fight them. In the final weeks of the race, Mr. Moussavi's campaign gained tremendous energy, and huge enthusiastic rallies packed the streets of Tehran day and night. His moderate views won him support from other reformers in Iran. The appearance of his wife, Zahra Rahnavard, actively campaigning alongside him drew women to his cause.</skos:definition>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/moussavi_mir_hussein_per"/>
  </rdf:Description>
