    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2006-09-26</nyt:first_use>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The National Journal's Almanac of American Politics 2008: Adapted from
John E. Sununu (R-New Hampshire), a Republican elected in 2002 when he defeated the state’s senior senator and its governor, was the youngest member of the Senate. He was defeated in his 2008 re-election bid by former governor Jeanne Shaheen. Mr. Sununu grew up in Salem, on the Massachusetts border, one of eight children of John H. Sununu, who was elected to the first of three terms as governor in 1982 and served as White House chief of staff from 1989 to 1991.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/s/john_e_sununu/index.html"/>
