    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The National Journal's Almanac of American Politics Adapted from
Pat Roberts, the state?s junior senator, is from a long Kansas Republican background. He graduated from Kansas State University, served four years in the Marine Corps, then spent five years running an Arizona newspaper.
Roberts acted as chief aide to 1st District Congressman Keith Sebelius for 12 years and won that seat with 56% in a three-candidate Republican primary after Sebelius retired in 1980. He spent 14 years in the minority in the House. In January 1995, after Republicans won their majority, Roberts became chairman of the House Agriculture Committee.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Roberts, Pat</skos:prefLabel>
  </rdf:Description>
