    <nyt:associated_article_count rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">113</nyt:associated_article_count>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.andy_pettitte"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated Oct.7, 2009
Andy Pettitte has quietly been one of the most successful pitchers of his era, ending the 2009 season with a career record of 229 wins and 135 losses. He is among an increasingly smaller group of Yankees who played together on all of the team's last four World Championships--a group that includes Derek Jeter, Mariano Rivera and Jorge Posada. A 15-year veteran, Pettitte has played for the Yankees for 12 seasons. He played for the Houston Astros in his native Texas from 2004 through 2006.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Pettitte, Andy</skos:prefLabel>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-12-10</nyt:latest_use>
