  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/N5161034656120955643">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated Sept. 4, 2009
Betsy McCaughey is a former Republican lieutenant governor of New York and an outspoken opponent of President Obama's effort to overhaul health care.
Ms. McCaughey has repeatedly argued that parts of the legislation would deliberately drive the elderly to early graves - a claim, though dismissed by Republicans and Democrats in Congress, and by the White House, that has remained a source of alarm.
For Ms. McCaughey, born on Oct. 20, 1948 in Pittsburgh, Pa., dismantling huge health care proposals by Democrats has been a career maker.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-11-15</nyt:latest_use>
