  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/59269220729064501813">
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/t/william_c_jr_thompson/index.html"/>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/thompson_william_c_jr_per"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: Nov. 5, 2009
William C. Thompson Jr., New York City comptroller and former Board of Education president, was the Democratic mayoral candidate in the 2009 election. On Nov. 3, in an unexpectedly close race, Mr. Thompson lost to Michael R. Bloomberg, who won a third term as New York City's 108th mayor. Election returns showed Mr. Bloomberg winning by only 5 percent.
Elected comptroller in 2001, when Mr. Bloomberg was elected mayor, Mr. Thompson had been an ally but also an occasional critic of Mr. Bloomberg. As the city's chief financial officer, Mr. Thompson has emphasized his watchdog role, frequently issuing audits about the management of city programs. He also oversees the city's pension funds, which total more than $80 billion; advises the mayor and the City Council on municipal finances; and leads a staff of more than 700 employees. He is to be replaced on Jan. 1, 2009, by John C. Liu, a Democratic councilman from Queens who was elected comptroller on Nov. 3.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">6</nyt:number_of_variants>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Thompson, William C Jr</skos:prefLabel>
