  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/69367370092737487383">
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.horst_kohler"/>
    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2008-03-19</nyt:first_use>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated May 26, 2009
a serious political blow. Angela Merkel Horst Köhler was re-elected president of Germany on May 23, 2009, by a single vote, eking out a narrow victory that spared Chancellor
The president is elected for a five-year term.  Mr. Köhler, Germany's ninth postwar president, first took office in July 2004.
Though the German presidency is a largely ceremonial position -- the president, chosen by members of the German Parliament and state representatives, serves as a kind of moral arbiter and international ambassador -- analysts view the secret ballot as an important test of party solidarity.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-05-24</nyt:latest_use>
