    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Weiner, Anthony D</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated May 26, 2009
Anthony D. Weiner is a United States congressman representing a district that includes neighborhoods in Brooklyn and Queens.
He was elected in 1998 to the congressional seat that had been held by Charles E. Schumer, Mr. Weiner’s political mentor and former boss. Mr. Schumer left the House of Representatives to run for the United States Senate. Before Mr. Weiner was elected to Congress, he was a member of the New York City Council, elected in 1991 when, at  27, he became the youngest person to serve in the Council up until that time.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
