    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Christopher Wheeldon, the dancer and founder of Morphoses/The Wheeldon Company, may well be the worldâ€™s most in-demand ballet choreographer.
Born in England in 1973, he trained at the Royal Ballet school and danced with both the Royal and City Ballet. At the age of 24 he returned to choreography full time, as a resident choreographer for New York City Ballet. It was there, during the companyâ€™s 2000-2001 season, that he became known as an innovator who honored balletâ€™s traditions while expanding its boundaries.
Critics routinely praise his wit and imagination and point to his keen musicality, mastery of stage space and inventive partnering. His best-known works â€” the strange and stirring â€œPolyphoniaâ€ (2001) and â€œAfter the Rainâ€ (2005) â€” gain their power through the force of their sensual shapes, lines and geometric forms.</skos:definition>
