  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/56467162509517015653">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">, Democrat of Massachusetts, said Mr. Hill was acting on instructions from the Bush White House in not pursuing human rights issues in talks with North Korea. The vote was 73 to 23. John Kerry , Republican of Kansas, assessed Mr. Hill's record on North Korea as "no progress on human rights, terrible deal, failed diplomacy." But Senator  Sam Brownback  on April 21st despite some Republicans' objections to his handling of talks with North Korea. Senator  Iraq  as the new ambassador to  Christopher R. Hill The United States Senate confirmed</skos:definition>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/hill_christopher_r_per"/>
