    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">1</nyt:number_of_variants>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.jerry_falwell"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Jerry Falwell 1933-2007
Jerry Falwell, the fundamentalist preacher who founded the Moral Majority and helped bring the language and passions of religious conservatives into American politics, died Tuesday, May 15, 2007, shortly after he was found unconscious in his office at Liberty University in Lynchburg, Va. He was 73 years old.
Mr. Falwell had a history of heart problems, and probably died of cardiac arrythmia, his physician, Dr. Carl Moore, said.
Read the full obituary.</skos:definition>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/falwell_jerry_per"/>
