    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Leonard, John</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">John Leonard, a widely influential and enduringly visible cultural critic, was known for the breadth of his knowledge, the depth of his inquiries and the lavish passion of his prose. Considered one of his profession?s most eminent practitioners, Mr. Leonard was the television critic for New York magazine and a regular book critic for Harper?s Magazine. For many years he was a cultural critic for ?CBS Sunday Morning.?
Read More...
Mr. Leonard had a long association with The New York Times. In the 1970s he was the editor of The Times Book Review and was afterward a cultural critic at the paper. A contributing editor of The Nation, Mr. Leonard was also a past literary editor there, a post he held jointly with his wife, Sue Leonard, from 1995 to 1998.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/l/john_leonard/index.html"/>
    <nyt:associated_article_count rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">2</nyt:associated_article_count>
    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2008-11-07</nyt:first_use>
  </rdf:Description>
