  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/N48096195238509304163">
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Beckham, David</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated July 22, 2009
David Beckham may not be the best soccer player in the world, but he is certainly the most recognizable.
For a man of humble, middle-class roots in London, Beckham has played for some of the game's biggest and most successful teams, including Manchester United and Real Madrid. He has traveled the world as an ambassador of the game and evolved into a brand through vigorous promotion -- he is married to a former member of the pop group the Spice Girls and he lent his name to the popular film "Bend It Like Beckham." As an extension of his commercial endorsement deals with companies such as Adidas and Armani, he accepted with missionary zeal a move in 2007 to the United States, and Major League Soccer, that extended his brand and planted him and his wife, Victoria, among the galaxy of stars in Los Angeles and environs.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2005-03-27</nyt:first_use>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
