  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/N52952857788896466463">
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">3</nyt:number_of_variants>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.william_j_bratton"/>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/b/william_j_bratton/index.html"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: Nov. 3, 2009
Regarded in law enforcement circles as one of the country’s most innovative police chiefs, William J. Bratton was named in 2007 to his second five-year term as chief of the Los Angeles Police Department. On Aug. 5, 2009, Mr. Bratton announced that he would leave the department after nearly seven years to lead a private international security firm, Altegrity Security Consulting, in New York.
Charlie Beck, a 32-year veteran of the department, is Mr. Bratton's replacement.</skos:definition>
