    <nyt:associated_article_count rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">11</nyt:associated_article_count>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: March 10, 2009
With Bill Maher." Time  series "Real  HBO Bill Maher is host of the
Mr. Maher was born in New York Jan. 20, 1956 to a nurse, Julie Berman Maher, and a radio announcer, Bill Maher Sr., who later became an NBC news editor. He graduated from Cornell University, majoring in English. Mr. Maher did his first standup gig the summer after his junior year at the New York comedy club, Catch a Rising Star.
Mr. Maher began appearing regularly at several New York comedy clubs, meeting young comedians like Jerry Seinfeld, Paul Reiser and Richard Belzer. In 1982, he appeared on the Tonight Show with the idol of his childhood, Johnny Carson, who invited him back 25 more times. The comedian also tried acting, landing roles in several mostly mediocre films.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/m/bill_maher/index.html"/>
