    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: Aug. 21, 2009
Venus Williams, an American professional tennis player known for her punishing ground strokes, oppressive court coverage and blistering serve, has been a finalist at Wimbledon eight times since 1999 and has won the tournament five times, most recently in 2008. She has been ranked No. 1 in the world, and in July 2009 was ranked No. 3.  
titles -- seven in singles, nine in women's doubles, and two in mixed doubles. In 2000, she became the first black woman, and only the second woman, to win Wimbledon, the U.S. Open, and Olympic medals in singles and doubles in the same year.   Grand Slam  in 1994, she has won 18  Women's Tennis Association tour Since joining the</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/williams_venus_per"/>
  </rdf:Description>
