    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated Dec. 4, 2009
Gary Locke is the Secretary of the Department of Commerce.Â  He has also been governor of Washington State.
governor in the United States. He served two terms before stepping down after the 2004 election, citing a desire to spend more time with his family. Born into an immigrant family living in public housing, Mr. Locke made it to Yale University and served as a prosecutor, state legislator and King County executive before his election as governor. first Chinese American 's election as Washington's governor in 1996 made him the   Mr. Locke   , a Republican from New Hampshire, withdrew his nomination citing philosophical differences with the president. Judd Gregg  of New Mexico dropped out because of a federal investigation into state contracting and Senator  Bill Richardson Mr. Locke, a Democrat, was the third choice for the Commerce Department after Gov.</skos:definition>
