  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/N3759921068495333893">
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/spector_phil_per"/>
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">1</nyt:number_of_variants>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: May 29, 2009
Phil Spector is a record producer whose early-1960's songs created a style dubbed the "wall of sound" that blended multilayered orchestral arrangements with guitars and drums. He was inducted in the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame in 1989. In 2004, he was charged with murder in the 2003 death of Lana Clarkson, an actress who had been found dead in Mr. Spector's home of what he said was a self-inflicted gunshot wound. A trial that began in 2006 ended in a mistrial; a second trial in the case began in October 2008.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Spector, Phil</skos:prefLabel>
