    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">on November 4, 2008. Kay Hagan Elizabeth Dole was unseated as Senator for North Carolina by
The National Journal's Almanac of American Politics 2008: Adapted from
Elizabeth Dole, former Secretary of Transportation and Secretary of Labor, former president of the American Red Cross and candidate for president, was elected senator from North Carolina in 2002. She grew up in Salisbury, in the Piedmont textile country between Charlotte and Greensboro. In 1962 she went to Harvard Law School. In 1975 she married Senator Bob Dole and campaigned with him when he was nominated for vice president in 1976.</skos:definition>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.elizabeth_dole"/>
