  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/N59388218642507311603">
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/c/chelsea_clinton/index.html"/>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-12-01</nyt:latest_use>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">At age 12, Chelsea Clinton appeared in Bill Clinton's ''Man From Hope'' video, testifying to his fatherly virtues. During the Monica Lewinsky scandal six years later, she was photographed hand in hand with her parents, seemingly holding the couple together.
When Hillary Rodham Clinton first ran for the Senate, Chelsea, then 20, crisscrossed New York State by her mother's side. She continued to appear on her parents' behalf, accompanying them on trips (to Aspen, Colo., Germany and Israel), fund-raising ( she helped bring in more than $20 million for her father's foundation in fall 2007) and playing a more glamorous version of her lifelong role: model daughter.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2005-11-10</nyt:first_use>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
