    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.jack_kemp"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">John French Kemp Jr., 1935-2009
Jack Kemp, the former football star turned congressman who with an evangelist's fervor moved the Republican Party to a commitment to tax cuts as the central focus of economic policy, died of cancer on May 2, 2009, at his home in Bethesda, Md. He was 73.
Born in Los Angeles in 1935, Mr. Kemp was secretary of housing and urban development under the first President George Bush and the Republican vice-presidential nominee in 1996. But his greatest legacy may stem from his years as a Buffalo congressman, especially 1978, when his argument for sharp tax cuts to promote economic growth became party policy, one that has endured to this day.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Kemp, Jack F</skos:prefLabel>
