    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">1</nyt:number_of_variants>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-12-16</nyt:latest_use>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: July 27, 2009
Asked what makes Roy Halladay the best pitcher in baseball, the Yankees slugger Mark Teixeira widened his eyes with respect and wonder: "All his pitches start in the same place and end in a different place."
Halladay is a Cy Young winning pitcher for the Toronto Blue Jays, and is considered by many of his peers to consistently be the best starter in baseball.
In July 2009 the Blue Jays' general manager J. P. Ricciardi acknowledged that he would listen to trade offers for the team's All-Star pitcher. The non-waiver trade deadline is July 31. Halladay is expected to be wearing another team's uniform by then.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
