    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: Sept. 23, 2009
, a Democrat of Montana, on what they promised would be a bipartisan bill for overhauling the health care system. Max Baucus  rode to the White House nearly three decades ago. In 2009, as the  senior Republican member of the Finance Committee, he worked with the committee's chairman, Senator  Ronald Reagan  of Iowa was among the Republican conservatives swept into the Senate on the wave that  Charles E. Grassley
, and he is on the defensive as he seeks a sixth term in 2010, no longer conservative enough for those back home in Iowa who style themselves the protectors of the Reagan legacy. Republican Party Mr. Grassley has often been at the center of creating major legislation. But the health care reform effort is anathema to the conservatives who dominate the</skos:definition>
