    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: Nov. 13, 2009
Gregory B. Craig, a well-known and politically well-connected Washington lawyer, was the first White House Counsel for the Obama administration.
On Nov. 13, 2009, the White House said that Mr. Craig was stepping down as counsel, a departure timed to coordinate with a Justice Department announcement that five terrorism suspects held in Guantánamo Bay, Cuba, would face trial in New York.
and detention policies, problems that have bedeviled the administration and generated fierce battles inside and outside the White House. interrogation 's top lawyer, Mr. Craig had been at the center of thorny decisions on the prison at Guantánamo Bay and  President Obama As</skos:definition>
