    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: April 10, 2009
Jesse L. Jackson Jr., Democrat of Illinois, is the United States representative for Chicago's South Side. Mr. Jackson, who is the son of the civil rights activist, was a national co-chairman for the Obama campaign.
as senator.)  Mr. Blagojevich was formally indicted in April 2009. Roland W. Burris  of Illinois, but the governor was arrested Dec. 9, 2008, by federal authorities and charged with corruption. A criminal complaint included an allegation that he conspired to profit from his authority to fill the vacant seat. (Before Mr. Blagojevich was removed from office by the Illinois Legislature, he appointed  Gov. Rod R. Blagojevich . The decision was expected to made by  Barack Obama He was also among the candidates mentioned by Chicago political analysts to fill the United States Senate seat vacated by</skos:definition>
