    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Berra, Yogi</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: April 16, 2009
Yogi Berra is a former major league catcher, coach and manager. He spent most of his career in New York with the Yankees and is the living embodiment of America's most famous professional sports team, an approachable and unpretentious Hall of Famer who represents a proud franchise not always associated with such qualities.
Mr. Berra, who was born to Italian immigrants in St. Louis on May 12, 1925, lived through the Great Depression, fought in World War II, played on 10 World Series champions, won three American League Most Valuable Player awards as a catcher and managed both the Yankees and the Mets into the World Series.</skos:definition>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
