    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Ledger, Heath</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">accidental overdose of prescription medications. Heath Ledger, the Australian actor, died in New York City on Jan. 22, 2008, from an
Mr. Ledger rose to fame for his role as a gay cowboy in "Brokeback Mountain,'' released in 2005, for which he was nominated for an Academy Award as best actor. On Feb. 22, 2009, he won an Oscar for best supporting actor prize for his performance as the Joker in "The Dark Knight," which was released after his death. Mr. Ledger's parents afterward said his Oscar statuette would be held in trust by the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences.</skos:definition>
