    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: Aug. 25, 2009
leaders confirmed the death. Taliban  drone airstrike, according to American and Pakistani officials. On Aug. 25, Pakistani  C.I.A. Baitullah Mehsud, the supreme leader of Pakistan's feared Taliban movement and the country's No. 1 enemy, is believed to have been killed on Aug. 5, 2009, in a
and Waliur Rehman, both top aides to Mr. Mehsud and said to be rivals to succeed him, called The Associated Press to say that their leader had died Aug. 23 of injuries from the airstrike in South Waziristan, near the Afghan border. Hakimullah Mehsud</skos:definition>
