  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/89153053701506014623">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated June 2, 2009
Barnett A. Slepian was an obstetrician who performed abortions in Buffalo, N.Y. He was fatally shot on Oct. 23, 1998, by James C. Kopp, an anti-abortion protester. Dr. Slepian was 52.
Dr. Slepian, who had a private practice in suburban Amherst, N. Y., was also the primary doctor at Buffalo GYN Womenservices, the only abortion clinic in downtown Buffalo. He worked 15 to 24 hours a week performing abortions for largely poor and low-wage clients. </skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Slepian, Barnett A</skos:prefLabel>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-06-02</nyt:latest_use>
