  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/63379070170706796133">
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Hsu, Norman</skos:prefLabel>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-09-30</nyt:latest_use>
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">1</nyt:number_of_variants>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.norman_hsu"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated May 8, 2009
Norman Hsu, a prominent Democratic donor, worked tirelessly as a political fund-raiser until it was discovered in 2007 that he was a fugitive from justice. In 1992 Mr. Hsu had failed to show up for sentencing for his role in a scheme to defraud investors.
On May 7, 2009, Mr. Hsu, pleaded guilty to 10 counts of mail and wire fraud in what the authorities said was a multimillion-dollar Ponzi scheme that had bilked investors nationwide.
Mr. Hsu admitted that he recruited victims for his scheme by falsely promising them high returns on investments, and then paid off early investors with money from later ones. But despite his guilty plea to the fraud scheme, Mr. Hsu continues to deny allegations of campaign finance fraud.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:associated_article_count rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">20</nyt:associated_article_count>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/h/norman_hsu/index.html"/>
