    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated Aug. 10, 2009
Marion S. Barry Jr. is a former four-term mayor of Washington, D.C., who is currently a member of its City Council.  In his third term as mayor, in 1990, he was caught on videotape by the F.B.I. using crack cocaine in a Washington hotel. He was subsequently convicted and served six months in federal prison for drug possession, but, in a surprising, perhaps amazing, political comeback, was again elected mayor in 1994. In 2009, Mr. Barry and his unique career were the subject of an HBO documentary, "The Nine Lives of Marion Barry."</skos:definition>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/barry_marion_s_jr_per"/>
