  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/20033070741956969143">
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Padavan, Frank</skos:prefLabel>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.frank_padavan"/>
    <nyt:associated_article_count rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">12</nyt:associated_article_count>
    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2004-09-05</nyt:first_use>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated Aug. 10, 2009
Frank Padavan, a state senator from Queens, is a Republican in a strongly Democratic district. He was first elected to the State Senate in 1972, defeating the Democratic incumbent on his first try for elected office.
Mr. Padavan is considered something of an institution in his district, which includes several northeastern Queens neighborhoods, among them Flushing, Bellerose and Whitestone.
He has a reputation for being relatively independent, breaking with Republican leadership on issues important to his constituents, as in his support of rent stabilization. He has made his mark on substantive issues, like groundbreaking 1978 legislation that made it easier to open community-based group homes for the mentally ill.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/p/frank_padavan/index.html"/>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">1</nyt:number_of_variants>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-09-11</nyt:latest_use>
