    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-11-21</nyt:latest_use>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated Nov. 20, 2009
Roland W. Burris, a former attorney general in Illinois, filled the Senate seat vacated by Barack Obama -- a position he won through a roller-coaster of political surprises and drama that was a sharp departure from a career in which he had been primarily seen as a competent civil servant who had lost more elections than he had won.
Mr. Burris announced in July 2009 that he would not seek election in 2010 to a full Senate term. The decision did not come as a surprise since he had not been raising much money or showing other signs of organizing a campaign.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
