    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: July 16, 2009
and steep recession stemming from a disintegrating housing sector, volatile financial markets and bank failures, resurgent inflation and widening job losses. credit crisis Henry M. Paulson Jr., the former head of Goldman Sachs and one of the firm’s most accomplished global deal makers, served as Treasury secretary under President George W. Bush. He led the administration’s struggle to contain a
in preventing a complete collapse of the financial system was success enough. Ben S. Bernanke . His supporters said that the work he did with Federal Reserve Chairman  bailed out After he left office, Mr. Paulson was criticized by some for moving slowly to respond to the crisis, for an overly ad-hoc approach to the serial implosion of banks in 2008 and for being overly generous to the financial institutions the government</skos:definition>
