    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated Aug. 18, 2009
officer, setting the stage for a criminal investigation. He died on Aug. 18, 2009. C.I.A. Robert D. Novak was a political columnist and cable television fixture whose scoops reached across five decades. His nickname, "the prince of darkness," was invoked with renewed fervor in 2003 when, acting on a tip, he revealed the name of a
At one point his column appeared in as many as 300 newspapers, and he was one of the first personalities to emerge on all-news cable television. CNN put him on the air its first weekend.</skos:definition>
