    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: July 7, 2009
, a former comedian and an author, was sworn in as the junior senator from Minnesota on July 7, 2009, almost 250 days after a photo-finish election that was followed by a lengthy recount and longer court battle, leaving many ordinary Minnesotans weary. Al Franken
. filibusters  column, giving the party at least symbolic control over Senate  Democratic Mr. Franken's belated victory puts 60 senators in the
. On every ground, the judicial panel rejected Mr. Coleman's claims of trial errors or constitutional violations, and decided that Mr. Franken's election should be certified by the state as valid. 32-page unanimous decision , conceded the election to Mr. Franken after the Minnesota Supreme Court declared Mr. Franken the winner in a  Norm Coleman His Republican opponent,</skos:definition>
