    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Almanac of American Politics Adapted from the National Journal's
The 18th Congressional District of New York contains the heart of suburban Westchester County and also crosses the Hudson River into Rockland County to Haverstraw. It includes a host of affluent suburbs, many within easy reach of Grand Central via the Metro North rail lines.
Historically, Westchester was a Republican county but today it is mostly Democratic, after a heavy influx of Jews who broke down many legal restrictions and other barriers to residence after World War II. Another reason is that on the cultural issues of greatest import, gun control and abortion, affluent suburbanites in America?s biggest metropolitan area have been strongly on the liberal side.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:associated_article_count rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">2</nyt:associated_article_count>
    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2008-02-03</nyt:first_use>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2008-04-07</nyt:latest_use>
