  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/79808263948351956393">
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">John A. Boehner, a Republican U.S. representative from Ohio, is the House minority leader in the 110th Congress. He was speaker of the House in 2006, elected in February of that year after the resignation of Tom DeLay, who was under criminal investigation. When the Democrats gained control of the House in the November midterm elections, Mr. Boehner was elected G.O.P. leader in the House.
He was first elected to Congress in 1990, representing a district that includes parts of the suburbs of Cincinnati and Dayton. As a member of Gang of Seven, a group of G.O.P. freshman reformers who demanded that the names of colleagues who had overdrafts at the House bank be made public, Mr. Boehner angered Congressional veterans.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2005-06-09</nyt:first_use>
