  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/N69935256432023805413">
    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2004-09-05</nyt:first_use>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/b/barry_bonds/index.html"/>
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">4</nyt:number_of_variants>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Barry Bonds, the all-time home run leader, was indicted in November 2007 on charges that he made false statements before a federal grand jury about his use of performance-enhancing drugs.
Three days before Bonds's trial was scheduled to begin on March 2, federal prosecutors appealed a judge's ruling that had eliminated several pieces of key evidence, including positive drug tests.
The appeal is still pending and Bonds's trial will likely not begin until the end of 2009 at the earliest.
Bonds had established himself as one of the game's best players before his power numbers surged at a point in his career when most players see a downturn in their skills. In 2001, at the age of 36, Bonds had one of the best offensive seasons in baseball history. He hit 73 home runs, breaking the single-season record for home runs, had 137 runs batted in, had a .328 batting average, a .515 on base percentage and a .863 slugging percentage.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Bonds, Barry</skos:prefLabel>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/bonds_barry_per"/>
