    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: Oct. 16, 2009
's shocking fall from power.  Upon taking office in 2008, Mr. Paterson became New York's first African-American governor. He is legally blind. Eliot Spitzer David A. Paterson is the governor of New York State. He was elected lieutenant governor in November 2006, a position with no power and little prestige, then propelled into the governorship by
Mr. Paterson's time as governor has not gone smoothly, and a series of missteps have raised questions about his ability to govern.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-12-30</nyt:latest_use>
