  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/17783906783903484983">
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/webb_james_h_jr_per"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Webb, James H Jr</skos:prefLabel>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.jim_webb"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Jim Webb, a military hero, successful author and former Navy secretary, was elected to the United States Senate from Virginia in 2006. A moderate Democrat in favor of gun ownership and limits on immigration, he was a Republican until he switched party affiliations over his opposition to President Bush's policies, primarily the war in Iraq.
Since his election, he has become a rising star in his party, giving the Democrats? blistering response to President Bush?s 2007 State of the Union address, and appearing regularly in debates on national news shows. He has been mentioned as a possible vice presidential contender in 2008 on the ticket with Barack Obama.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-09-05</nyt:latest_use>
