    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated Oct. 7, 2009
Derek Jeter is the shortstop and captain of the New York Yankees. He is an all-star, a most valuable player and, increasingly, one whose name is spoken in the adoring tones reserved mostly for players with names like Ruth, Gehrig or Mantle.
On Sept. 11, 2009, Jeter hit a hard single to right field-with his patented inside-out swing-against the Baltimore Orioles, and broke Lou Gehrig's Yankee record for career hits with number 2,722. The all-time hit leader in Major League Baseball is Pete Rose, who banged out 4,256 hits in a 23-year career. Jeter has played 14 seasons, all with the Yankees.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">1</nyt:number_of_variants>
