    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/domingo_placido_per"/>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.placido_domingo"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/d/placido_domingo/index.html"/>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-11-04</nyt:latest_use>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: March 12, 2009
If you start with his professional debut in Mexico at 16, singing as a baritone in the zarzuela company his family ran, Plácido Domingo has been before the public for 52 years. In an astonishingly long career, including 40 seasons with the Metropolitan Opera, Mr. Domingo said that he can not see himself retiring the way many star singers do: by announcing a farewell tour and going from company to company, city to city, accepting tributes and taking his leave.  "Rather," he said, "I think it will be one evening, after a performance, to say, 'That's it.' "</skos:definition>
    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2004-10-20</nyt:first_use>
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">2</nyt:number_of_variants>
    <nyt:associated_article_count rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">31</nyt:associated_article_count>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Domingo, Placido</skos:prefLabel>
  </rdf:Description>
