  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/49210931799785510563">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated March 28, 2009
By Mel Gussow
Ionesco's wildly innovative plays, among them "Rhinoceros," "The Bald Soprano" and "The Chairs," overturned conventions of contemporary theater and had a profound effect on a new generation of playwrights. He died on March 28, 1994, at 84 in Paris, where he lived.  Eugène
A revival of his 1962 play "Exit the King" opened on Broadway on March 26, 2009, starring Geoffrey Rush and Susan Sarandon. Ben Brantley in The Times called the revival "brutally funny" and said that Mr. Rush's performance's was like "a fire-trailing comet."</skos:definition>
    <nyt:associated_article_count rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">5</nyt:associated_article_count>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
