    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: March 23, 2009
in physics, also has impeccable credentials in science management. Nobel Prize Steven Chu, a Nobel Prize-winning experimental physicist, is secretary of energy in the Obama administration. Dr. Chu, who shared the 1997
. climate change  has assigned Dr. Chu to carry out some of his central priorities: wean America from dependence on fossil fuels, rebuild the nation's electrical grid and address the challenges of  President Obama
Dr. Chu served as chairman of the physics department at Stanford, and head of the electronics research laboratory at Bell Labs. He shared the 1997 Nobel in physics for his work on cooling and trapping atoms with laser light.</skos:definition>
