    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/t/george_r_tiller/index.html"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated July 27, 2009
George Tiller was the nation's pre-eminent abortion practitioner, drawing women to Wichita from all over with his willingness to perform late-term abortions, hundreds each year. For more than 30 years the anti-abortion movement threw everything into driving Dr. Tiller out of business, certain that his defeat would deal a devastating blow to the "abortion industry" that has terminated roughly 50 million pregnancies since Roe v. Wade in 1973.
Dr. Tiller was shot to death in Wichita, Kan., May 31, 2009, in the foyer of his longtime church as he handed out the church bulletin.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Tiller, George R</skos:prefLabel>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.george_tiller"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-03-28</nyt:first_use>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
  </rdf:Description>
