  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/51565115083476142123">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">George Michael was one of the biggest pop stars of the 1980s, first as one half of "Wham!" and then on his own with the worldwide hit album "Faith." Born Georgios Kyriacos Panayiotou in north London, the son of Greek immigrants, Mr. Michael has sold more than 80 million records, according to his Web site, georgemichael.com.
As a teenager, Mr. Michael teamed up with Andrew Ridgeley to form "Wham!," which is best known for hits like "Wake Me Up Before You Go Go" and "Careless Whisper." The group?s style was British teeny-bopper pop, laced with soul, and Mr. Michael, the duo's front man, cultivated a sexy-but-sensitive image.</skos:definition>
