  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/80854242758935355333">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated July 9, 2009
Pedro Espada Jr. set off a five week-long deadlock in the New York State Senate when he and Hiram Monserrate, both Democrats, threw their support behind the Republican senators on June 8, 2009. The move seemed to end the Democrats' short-lived control under Senator Malcolm A. Smith. While Mr. Espada and Mr. Monserrate said they were forming a bipartisan power-sharing deal, the arrangement effectively reestablished Republican control.
But after a week of chaos in the state capital, Mr. Monserrate switched his allegiances again, and  reaffirmed himself as a member of the Democratic caucus.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">5</nyt:number_of_variants>
