  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/53633337485236611813">
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Waxman, Henry A</skos:prefLabel>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-08-26</nyt:latest_use>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">In November 2008, Representative Henry A. Waxman, Democrat of California, unseated Representative John Dingell to become chairman of the powerful House Energy and Commerce Committee. The 255-member House Democratic conference voted 137 to 122 to accept the recommendation of its steering committee and agreed to replace Mr. Dingell, 82, a long-time friend of the U.S. auto industry, with Mr. Waxman, a 69-year-old Californian anxious to ease global warming, a top concern of President-elect Barack Obama.
Mr. Waxman has been chairman of the Committee on Oversight and Government Reform, and was a key figure in congressional hearings on steroid use in baseball, and the testimony of Roger Clemens.</skos:definition>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.henry_waxman"/>
