    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">2</nyt:number_of_variants>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/r/francisco_rodriguez/index.html"/>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Francisco Rodriguez, who holds the major league record for saves in a season, signed with the Mets as a free agent in December 2008. Rodriguez joined a bullpen that was one of the worst in baseball in 2008, and contributed greatly to the Mets' second consecutive late-season collapse. He is coming off a season in which he saved 62 games for the Los Angeles Angels. His saves total smashed the previous record, 57, which had been set by Bobby Thigpen of the Chicago White Sox in 1990.
Rodriguez was promoted to the major leagues in September 2002. The Angels recalled him on Sept. 15 -- 15 days after the deadline to qualify for the postseason roster -- but he sneaked onto the playoff roster after another pitcher was injured, a fortuitous twist of fate that led the Angels to their first World Series championship. He did not become the Angels' full-time closer until 2005, and he saved a combined 132 games over that and the next two seasons.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Rodriguez, Francisco</skos:prefLabel>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/rodriguez_francisco_per"/>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.francisco_rodriguez"/>
