    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.stephen_colbert"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated June 12, 2009
Stephen Colbert is the host of Comedy Central's "The Colbert Report," a parody of Fox News-style cable opinion shows. Mr. Colbert plays the part of an obtuse, pompous arch conservative.
Mr. Colbert's audience on Comedy Central isn't very large (a little over a million on a good day), but he has cachet with young and would-be hip viewers who get most of their news from iPhone applications, blogs and comedy shows.
Before hosting "The Colbert Report," Mr. Colbert was a correspondent on the fake news digest "The Daily Show."</skos:definition>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/c/stephen_colbert/index.html"/>
    <nyt:associated_article_count rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">44</nyt:associated_article_count>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Colbert, Stephen</skos:prefLabel>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/colbert_stephen_per"/>
  </rdf:Description>
