    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated Oct. 23, 2009
Isiah Thomas is the basketball coach at Florida International University and a retired National Basketball Association point guard of the Detroit Pistons. He previously coached the New York Knicks and Indiana Pacers.
Mr. Thomas played for the Pistons from 1981- 1994 and was elected to the NBA Hall of Fame in 2000 on the first ballot. He was also named one of the National Basketball Association's 50 greatest players. He led the Detroit Pistons to back-to-back NBA titles in 1988-89 and 1989-90.
Isiah Lord Thomas III was born April 30, 1961 in Chicago the youngest of nine brothers and sisters. He played college basketball at Indiana University under coach Bob Knight and led his team to the National Championship in 1981. He was named the NCAA tournament's Most Outstanding Player.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
