    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/james_lebron_per"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: June 1, 2009
LeBron James, dubbed "The Chosen One" on the cover of Sports Illustrated in 2002 when he was a 17-year-old high school player in Ohio, James was the No. 1 pick in the 2003 N.B.A. draft. His presence revitalized the Cleveland Cavaliers and renewed fan interest. He was the N.B.A.'s rookie of the year in 2003-4, and is a four-time All-Star and a two-time All-Star Game most valuable player. He was voted the N.B.A.'s most valuable player for the 2008-9 season.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">James, LeBron</skos:prefLabel>
