  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/78148964787618726903">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated May 8, 2009
Bob Kerrey, a former governor and United States senator from Nebraska, has been president of the New School University in Greenwich Village since 2001, raising the school's profile while also running afoul of some faculty and students.
On May 6, 2009, after a year marked by criticism and student protests, he announced that he would step down when his contract expires on July 1, 2011.
Mr. Kerrey, who lost half his right leg in Vietnam, sought the Democratic presidential nomination in 1992 and flirted with a repeat run in 2000; he also briefly considered running for Mayor of New York City in 2005, a year after he returned to the national spotlight as a member of the commission that investigated the Sept. 11 terrorist attacks.</skos:definition>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
