    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Williams, Brian</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: March 9, 2009
Brian Williams had what some saw as the unenviable task of succeeding Tom Brokaw as anchor of ''Nightly News'' in 2004, a position he held for 21 years. Among the many expectations NBC established for Mr. Williams was that he maintain the program's standing as the top-rated of the three network evening newscasts, extending a lead his predecessor held for the last eight years.
Until the fall of 2008, the NBC ''Nightly News'' had been in a tight race with ABC's "World News." In early March Mr. Williams's newscast finished first for 20 consecutive weeks, with about 9.5 million viewers, roughly a million more than ABC. (''The CBS Evening News With Katie Couric'' trailed the pack with two million to three million fewer viewers than NBC's program.)</skos:definition>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/w/brian_williams/index.html"/>
  </rdf:Description>
