  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/48734851574728778413">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2004-09-23</nyt:first_use>
    <nyt:search_api_query rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://api.nytimes.com/svc/search/v1/article?query=+nytd_per_facet%3A%5BMaazel%2C+Lorin%5D&amp;rank=newest&amp;fields=abstract,author,body,byline,classifiers_facet,column_facet,date,day_of_week_facet,des_facet,desk_facet,fee,geo_facet,lead_paragraph,material_type_facet,multimedia,nytd_byline,nytd_des_facet,nytd_geo_facet,nytd_lead_paragraph,nytd_org_facet,nytd_per_facet,nytd_section_facet,nytd_title,nytd_works_mentioned_facet,org_facet,page_facet,per_facet,publication_day,publication_month,publication_year,section_page_facet,small_image_height,small_image_url,small_image_width,source_facet,title,url,word_count,works_mentioned_facet</nyt:search_api_query>
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">1</nyt:number_of_variants>
    <nyt:associated_article_count rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">69</nyt:associated_article_count>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/m/lorin_maazel/index.html"/>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: June 23, 2009
Lorin Maazel is the 24th conductor to hold the position of music director, or its equivalent, at the New York Philharmonic. He is the third American to hold that position, after Urelli Corelli Hill, its first director, and Leonard Bernstein, its 19th. Mr. Maazel finished his last season with the orchestra in June 2009; his successor, Alan Gilbert, will be the fourth American named to the job.
Mr. Maazel, who was a child prodigy, has held many important directorships in the United States and Europe and in both the symphonic and the operatic worlds. His huge discography covers all the peaks of the symphonic and operatic literature. Mozart, Beethoven, Mahler, Sibelius and Richard Strauss -- long staples in the Philharmonic diet -- are among his specialties. He virtually always conducts from memory, with a kinetic podium style and forceful interpretive personality. He is also a violinist and a composer who writes in a conservative style.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Maazel, Lorin</skos:prefLabel>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.lorin_maazel"/>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-07-14</nyt:latest_use>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/maazel_lorin_per"/>
  </rdf:Description>
