  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/6857933236772706463">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The National Journal's Almanac of American Politics 2008: Adapted from
Jim Bunning, a Republican elected to the Senate in 1998, is the first player elected to the Baseball Hall of Fame to serve in Congress. He made the majors in 1956 and the next year became the only pitcher to strike out Ted Williams three times in one game. Bunning threw a no-hitter for the Detroit Tigers in 1958 and pitched a perfect game for the Philadelphia Phillies on Fatherâ€™s Day 1964; he also played for the Pittsburgh Pirates and the Los Angeles Dodgers.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2005-03-24</nyt:first_use>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
