  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/66465943023589187743">
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-02-12</nyt:latest_use>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/s/anna_sui/index.html"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: Feb. 12, 2009
almost before the British singer and It Girl was born. Lily Allen It has been many seasons since Anna Sui first showed clothes on a runway, starting in 1991 when she unveiled a feminine style that evokes an addled ingénue unafraid of a drink or of letting her knickers show:
The clothes in Ms. Sui’s first show were modeled by pals, among them Linda Evangelista and Naomi Campbell. That those professional beauties were then at the height of their fame helped stoke the reception the designer got from buyers and the news media, and it also insured industry embrace of a talented designer who had, until then, been working quietly and anonymously on other people’s lines.</skos:definition>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.anna_sui"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
