    <nyt:search_api_query rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://api.nytimes.com/svc/search/v1/article?query=+nytd_per_facet%3A%5BRegan%2C+Judith%5D&amp;rank=newest&amp;fields=abstract,author,body,byline,classifiers_facet,column_facet,date,day_of_week_facet,des_facet,desk_facet,fee,geo_facet,lead_paragraph,material_type_facet,multimedia,nytd_byline,nytd_des_facet,nytd_geo_facet,nytd_lead_paragraph,nytd_org_facet,nytd_per_facet,nytd_section_facet,nytd_title,nytd_works_mentioned_facet,org_facet,page_facet,per_facet,publication_day,publication_month,publication_year,section_page_facet,small_image_height,small_image_url,small_image_width,source_facet,title,url,word_count,works_mentioned_facet</nyt:search_api_query>
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">1</nyt:number_of_variants>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2008-01-26</nyt:latest_use>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">during his bid to become homeland security secretary in late 2004. Bernard B. Kerik Judith Regan, the publisher and editor, has long been considered the public face of the book industry's most nakedly commercial wing. After she came to prominence as the editor of best-selling books by writers like Howard Stern and Rush Limbaugh, Rupert Murdoch hired Ms. Regan to start her own imprint ? ReganBooks ? as part of News Corporation's HarperCollins, a major book publisher. She ran the imprint from 1994 until she was fired in 2006, producing a string of successful books, many on subjects few others would touch. Ms. Regan's firing followed the uproar surrounding ReganBooks's plans to publish O.J. Simpson's "If I Did It." On November 13, 2007 Ms. Regan asserted in a lawsuit that a senior executive at the media conglomerate encouraged her to mislead federal investigators about her relationship with</skos:definition>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/r/judith_regan/index.html"/>
    <nyt:associated_article_count rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">25</nyt:associated_article_count>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Regan, Judith</skos:prefLabel>
  </rdf:Description>
