    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/s/gordon_h_smith/index.html"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">National Journal's Almanac of American Politics Adapted from the
Gordon Smith, former Oregon senator, was first elected to the Senate in 1996. He  was born in Pendleton and grew up in the Washington suburbs.
He graduated from Brigham Young and from law school in Los Angeles, was a law clerk in New Mexico and practiced law in Arizona. Then he bought the family frozen vegetable processing company, Smith Frozen Foods, in Pendleton, and guided it out of debt to profitability.
In 1992 he was elected to the state Senate and in 1995 became Senate president.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
