    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2006-02-11</nyt:first_use>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Domenici, Pete V</skos:prefLabel>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/d/pete_v_domenici/index.html"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Over a career of 36 years, Pete V. Domenici of New Mexico became not only one of the most senior Republicans in Congress but a power on energy and budget issues. Before his retirement, he also became a central figure in the congressional inquiry into the firing of United States attorneys, including one based in Albuquerque.
For 22 years, Mr. Domenici was the chairman or ranking lawmaker on the Senate Budget Committee. In the 1980's and 90's, he was known as perhaps the most prominent "deficit hawk'' in the Senate. And as a leading Republican on the Energy and Natural Resources Committee, he was a strong advocate for nuclear power and helped broker major energy legislation in recent years. Over the years, Mr. Domenici was also an advocate for parity in insurance coverage for mental health, a position shaped by the experience of one of his daughters, who has schizophrenia.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
