    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.michael_strahan"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Michael Strahan, a defensive end, was a longtime leader of the Giants? defense and is considered a likely first-ballot Hall of Famer. He retired from from the N.F.L. on June 10, 2008, leaving his lone Super Bowl victory as the final game of a 15-year career.
Strahan retired as the Giants? leader in games played (216 in the regular season) and sacks (141 Â½). He was named to the Pro Bowl seven times, and set the league?s single-season sack record in 2001, with 22 Â½. He won numerous defensive player of the year awards.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2004-09-27</nyt:first_use>
