    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.sonia_sotomayor"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: Aug. 6, 2009  |  OVERVIEW
Sonia Sotomayor is an associate justice for the Supreme Court, the first Hispanic justice in the court's history, and only its third woman. On Aug. 8,2009, Chief Justice John G. Roberts Jr. administered a pair of oaths to her in two private ceremonies at the Supreme Court building, completing her ascent to a life-tenured position as the nationâ€™s 111th justice.
Ms. Sotomayor was a judge of the United States Court of Appeals for the Second Circuit when President Obama nominated her in May 2009 to replace the retiring Justice David H. Souter. Before joining the appeals court in 1998, she served as a United States District Court judge for the Southern District of New York.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
