    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Gene Upshaw, the longtime head of the N.F.L. players association and a member of the Pro Football Hall of Fame, died of pancreatic cancer on Aug. 21, 2008.
Born in 1945 in Robstown, Tex., Upshaw was a first-round selection by the Oakland Raiders in 1967, the first draft by the N.F.L. and the American Football League. Upshaw was a guard for the Raiders for 15 years, and he played in three Super Bowls. He played in 307 games, including three A.F.L. and seven A.F.C. championship games. He was the first person to play guard exclusively who was voted into the Hall of Fame.</skos:definition>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.gene_upshaw"/>
  </rdf:Description>
