    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.mike_dantoni"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Mike D?Antoni left the Phoenix Suns in May 2008 to join the Knicks ? trading an All-Star lineup for a roster of misfits, leaving perhaps the league?s most stable franchise for perhaps its most dysfunctional.
Like anyone who achieves quick fame and adulation, D?Antoni has become saddled by his own reputation. He is known as an innovator and an entertainer, an advocate of shooting the ball in seven seconds or less, an evangelist of high-octane basketball, a true believer that a fast-and-furious offense can trump a great defense.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">D'Antoni, Mike</skos:prefLabel>
    <nyt:associated_article_count rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">97</nyt:associated_article_count>
