    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: June 30, 2009
draft, Shaquille O'Neal has been among the most imposing, skillful and physically dominant centers in the history of the league, a daunting low post presence forcing adjustments, reassessments and revisions from coast to coast. National Basketball Association Since he was chosen first over all in the 1992
.   Miami Heat , in 2000, 2001 and 2002, and most recently in 2006, with the  Los Angeles Lakers He has played on four N.B.A. championship teams, three while with the
on June 25, 2009, in a stunning trade that had immediate ramifications across the league. Phoenix Suns , in a bold stroke aimed at winning the championship, acquired O'Neal from the  Cleveland Cavaliers The</skos:definition>
