  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/N31113414111409292123">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Richard Shelby, Alabama?s senior senator, has had a political career going back more than 30 years.
Mr. Shelby was elected state senator in 1970, and won a House seat in 1978.
In the House, Mr. Shelby had a conservative voting record, opposing the Voting Rights Act extension and the Martin Luther King Holiday. He ran for the Senate in 1986 and won by 7,000 votes.
As one of half a dozen or so conservative southern Democrats in the Senate, Mr. Shelby at first attracted little notice.</skos:definition>
