    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: Nov. 19, 2009
Eric H. Holder Jr. is the attorney general, appointed by President Obama. He served as deputy attorney general under Janet Reno during the Clinton administration.
, who resigned in 2007, the department was run as a satellite office of the White House. A series of internal reports concluded that politics improperly interfered in areas like the hiring of low- and mid-level personnel, and Mr. Gonzales was sharply criticized in Congress for the firing of prosecutors on what many senators said was political grounds. Alberto R. Gonzales Mr. Holder inherited a Justice Department that was deeply demoralized. Lawmakers in both parties have said that under</skos:definition>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/h/eric_h_holder_jr/index.html"/>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-12-10</nyt:latest_use>
  </rdf:Description>
