    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Valentine, Bobby</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: May 21, 2009
Bobby Valentine, a former major league baseball player and manager for the Texas Rangers and the Mets, is the popular manager for the Chiba Lotte Marines in Japan.
He was a highly regarded high school athlete from Stamford, Conn., who reached the major leagues in 1969 as a 19-year-old with the Los Angeles Dodgers. He played 10 seasons in the majors with the Dodgers, California Angels, San Diego Padres, Mets and Seattle Mariners, but his promising career was cut short because of injuries.</skos:definition>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/valentine_bobby_per"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
