    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/kagan_robert_per"/>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Robert Kagan, a senior associate at the Carnegie Endowment for International Peace, emerged in the Bush years as a leading architect of a muscular and expansive American policy.
Though he started as an official and speechwriter in the State Department in the Reagan administration, Mr. Kagan became influential through his books and articles, not through positions in government. Long associated with The Weekly Standard and its editor, William Kristol, Mr. Kagan writes a monthly foreign affairs column for The Washington Post and is also a contributing editor to The New Republic.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2004-12-17</nyt:first_use>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Kagan, Robert</skos:prefLabel>
