    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: Sept. 14, 2009
By Stephanie Rosenbloom
. Smithsonian Institution body-hugging wrap dress so emblematic of 1970s fashion that it hangs in the  Diane von Furstenberg is a top American fashion designer. She is the creator of the
. Jennifer Lopez Ms. von Furstenberg has had two separate fashion careers. Her business skyrocketed in the 1970s, crashed in the '80s and, unpredictably, is thriving today. In the 1990s, a new generation of women discovered her clingy print dresses in vintage shops, prompting the resurrection of the brand. Today the dresses are worn by women like Jessica Alba, Madonna and</skos:definition>
