  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/85994189373752780253">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.tim_tebow"/>
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">1</nyt:number_of_variants>
    <nyt:associated_article_count rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">40</nyt:associated_article_count>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Sept. 10, 2009
As a quarterback at the University of Florida, Tim Tebow won the Heisman Trophy in 2007 as the sport's top player and helped the Gators win the national championship in the 2006 and 2008 seasons.
Tebow's on-field performances have entered him into the conversation about college football's greats. From TMZ.com to maximum-security prisons where he preaches to the buckle of the Bible Belt, Tebow has achieved something rare for a college athlete - he has crossed over into popular culture.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2007-09-16</nyt:first_use>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-12-09</nyt:latest_use>
