    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2004-10-10</nyt:first_use>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-11-06</nyt:latest_use>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated Oct. 7, 2009
Mariano Rivera is an all-star relief pitcher for the New York Yankees, and the all-time leader in saves in the American League. He became just the second pitcher in baseball history to save 500 games when he preserved a win over the cross-town rival Mets, 4-2, on June 28, 2009. (He also collected his first ever run batted in when he walked with the bases loaded in the ninth inning.)
Only Trevor Hoffman, of the Milwaukee Brewers in the National League, has recorded more saves than Rivera. At the end of the 2009 regular season, Hoffman had 591 saves to Rivera's 526.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
