  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/N10528848271449221383">
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">DeGeneres, Ellen</skos:prefLabel>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/degeneres_ellen_per"/>
    <nyt:associated_article_count rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">16</nyt:associated_article_count>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-11-15</nyt:latest_use>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated Sept. 11, 2009
In September 2009, Ellen DeGeneres was named the fourth judge of the "American Idol," the Fox talent competition. She replaces Paula Abdul, who announced in July that she would leave the show.
Ms. DeGeneres vowed to fill Ms. Abdul's role as the nice one while also offering the perspective of fans at home.
"I'm not going to be mean," Ms. DeGeneres said. Referring to Simon Cowell, the British judge who usually offers the most piercing criticisms of "Idol" contestants, she added: "I hate when Simon's that mean. You can be constructive and you can criticize somebody in a way that's helpful instead of meanspirited."</skos:definition>
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">2</nyt:number_of_variants>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/d/ellen_degeneres/index.html"/>
    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2004-10-13</nyt:first_use>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.ellen_degeneres"/>
