    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: Oct. 12, 2009
Carly Simon, one of pop music's most notoriously stage-shy performers, is a Grammy-winning singer and composer.
in 1972 (they later divorced) inspired "You Belong to Me"; by the 1980s her songs were more pop-driven, like "Coming Around Again" and "Let the River Run," which won an Oscar for best song in 1989. James Taylor Her first hit, "That's the Way I've Always Heard It Should Be," came out in 1971. Her marriage to
