    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">1</nyt:number_of_variants>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: July 27, 2009
By Alastair Macaulay
Medallion. To that audience he recalled, as he has on other occasions, how he arrived in New York for the first time in September 1939, by train, ready to join Martha Graham's company as its second male dancer: "I stepped onto the sidewalk, took one look at the skyline and thought, 'This is home.' " Handel The choreographer Merce Cunningham died on July 26, 2009. He was 90. Almost 10 years before, on the stage of the New York State Theater, he was awarded the city's highest cultural award, the</skos:definition>
    <nyt:associated_article_count rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">47</nyt:associated_article_count>
