  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/N35413515894560920283">
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/b/plaxico_burress/index.html"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Burress, Plaxico</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated Aug. 21, 2009
Plaxico Burress, a talented but controversial receiver, helped the New York Giants win Super Bowl XLII in 2008  with a game-winning touchdown catch. But in early August 2009, he was indicted on weapons charges related to an incident in November 2008, when he accidentally shot himself in the thigh in a Manhattan nightclub. On Aug. 20, 2009, he pleaded guilty in a deal with Manhattan prosecutors that will send him to prison for two years.
The Giants had released him from the team in April 2009 without waiting for the outcome of the case. Along with the two-year prison sentence, Burress will be sentenced to two years of post-release supervision.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-10-11</nyt:latest_use>
