    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.anne_hathaway"/>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
    <nyt:associated_article_count rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">13</nyt:associated_article_count>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/hathaway_anne_per"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated June 25, 2009
Anne Hathaway, a graduate of Millburn High School in New Jersey, made her movie breakthrough in 2001 in her first film role, opposite Julie Andrews in “The Princess Diaries.” The Brooklyn-born Ms. Hathaway played Mia Thermopolis, a run-of-the-mill San Francisco prep school student who suddenly learns that the late father she never knew was the prince of the Monaco-like country of Genovia and that she is now the crown princess.
The critic Elvis Mitchell in The New York Times called her “a young comic talent” with “charisma that recalls Julia Roberts.”</skos:definition>
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">1</nyt:number_of_variants>
  </rdf:Description>
