  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/N19097679281564458873">
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Christopher Buckley, a political satirist, magazine editor and journalist, is best known as the author of comic novels about Washington's power elite, especially his farcical take on the tobacco lobby, "Thank You for Smoking" (1994), which was adapted into a 2005 film.
The son of the late William F. Buckley Jr., Mr. Buckley was a speechwriter for George H. W. Bush. He is a libertarian-leaning conservative, but his personal politics have never stopped him from lampooning Republicans as viciously as Democrats in his novels and opinion columns.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Buckley, Christopher</skos:prefLabel>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-05-03</nyt:latest_use>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/buckley_christopher_per"/>
