  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/20503309626378870743">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">After several seasons as an assistant coach with the New England Patriots under Bill Belichick, Eric Mangini took the head coaching job with the New York Jets in January 2006 and quickly turned the team into playoff contenders. The Jets were 10-6 in Mangini’s first season and he was named A.F.C. Coach of the Year.
. Miami Dolphins  him on Dec. 29, 2008, hours after the team completed a late-season swoon and was eliminated from playoff contention with a loss at home to the  Jets Yet his early successes would not last and after three of the four seasons of his contract, Mangini, 37, had a record of 23-26. The</skos:definition>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-11-22</nyt:latest_use>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">2</nyt:number_of_variants>
