    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.howard_dean"/>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/dean_howard_per"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Howard Dean, a former a governor of Vermont, became chairman of the Democratic National Committee after a bid for the presidency that failed but stirred new levels of support at the grass roots and on the Internet.
On Nov. 10, 2008, Mr. Dean announced that he would not seek a second term as chairman. His tenure marked by an aggressive attempt to reshape and expand the party's reach through what he called a 50-state strategy, and by frequent quarrels with the party's established Washington hierarchy, which favored a more conservative approach that focused on traditionally Democratic areas.</skos:definition>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
