    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-09-20</nyt:latest_use>
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">1</nyt:number_of_variants>
    <nyt:associated_article_count rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">261</nyt:associated_article_count>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated Sept. 21, 2009
John Edwards served as a one-term senator, came close to being elected vice president in 2004 and ran a credible campaign for the Democratic presidential nomination in 2008.
Once the favorite son of much of North Carolina with many supporters beyond, Mr. Edwards is now largely disdained because of his elaborate effort to cover up an extramarital affair to preserve his political ambitions. A federal grand jury is currently investigating whether any crimes were committed in connection with campaign laws in an effort to conceal his affair with Rielle Hunter.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
