  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/N49738820677371914643">
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/yudhoyono_susilo_bambang_per"/>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/y/susilo_bambang_yudhoyono/index.html"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated August 10, 2009
Susilo Bambang Yudhoyono, 59, is a retired general and the president of Indonesia. In July 2009 he became the first Indonesian president ever re-elected, winning in a landslide. It was only the second time that Indonesians have directly chosen their president. More than 120 million people cast ballots across the country, which emerged from three decades of military rule barely 10 years ago. Mr. Yudhoyono captured 61 percent of the vote, winning all but 5 of Indonesia’s 33 provinces.
Mr. Yudhoyono rose to prominence during the era of military rule under the late President Suharto, which lasted for 32 years, until 1998, but he has come to be viewed as the leader most capable of extricating Indonesia from that past.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">1</nyt:number_of_variants>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Yudhoyono, Susilo Bambang</skos:prefLabel>
