    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2005-01-07</nyt:first_use>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: Sept. 17, 2009
Senator Max Baucus (born 1941) is the chairman of the Senate Finance Committee, a position that has given the Montana Democrat a lead role on the health care and tax issues on President Obama's agenda.
Even before Mr. Obama's election, Mr. Baucus indicated that overhauling health policies would be his priority -- ''the challenge of my career,'' he said in an interview. He has spent more than half his life in Congress; he won the first of six Senate terms in 1978, after four years in the House.</skos:definition>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.max_baucus"/>
  </rdf:Description>
