    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated Oct. 15, 2009
, and set off a deadlock in Albany that lasted until both men eventually shifted their allegiances back to the Democrats. Malcolm A. Smith , both Democrats, threw their support behind the Republican senators. The move ended the Democrats' control in the Senate under Senator  Pedro Espada Jr. Hiram Monserrate is a Democratic state senator from Queens whose district includes East Elmhurst, Jackson Heights and Corona. On June 8, 2009, he and
In September 2009, just as Mr. Monserrate's starring role in Albany's political drama was fading from the headlines, his legal battles in an assault trial entered a new round. Mr. Monserrate was arrested on Dec. 19, 2008, shortly after his companion, Karla Giraldo, 30, appeared at Long Island Jewish Medical Center bleeding and distraught, saying he had attacked her at his home, according to court documents.</skos:definition>
