    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Coleman, Norm</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: June 30, 2009
Norm Coleman served one term representing Minnesota in the United States Senate. After losing the November 2008 election in one of the closest elections in the history of the Senate, Mr. Coleman has spent eight months locked in a court battle with Al Franken, his Democratic challenger.
, the judicial panel rejected Mr. Coleman's claims of trial errors or constitutional violations, and decided that Mr. Franken's election should be certified by the state as valid. 32-page unanimous decision On June 30, the Minnesota Supreme Court issued a judgment in the Senate race, declaring Mr. Franken the winner. In a</skos:definition>
    <nyt:associated_article_count rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">28</nyt:associated_article_count>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
