    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.john_cornyn"/>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">1</nyt:number_of_variants>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/c/john_cornyn/index.html"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated June 5, 2009
Senator John Cornyn, a Texan, is chairman of the National Republican Senatorial Committee. He is also a member of the Judiciary Committee.
Mr. Cornyn was elected to a second term in 2008 in a difficult year for his party. He was first elected in 2002 in a Senate race for the seat vacated by Phil Gramm. He quickly established a reputation as a determined partisan.
Mr. Cornyn had run as a supporter of George W. Bush, and of making the 2001 tax cuts permanent, extending the research and development tax credit and raising Texas's share of gas tax funds from 90.5 cents to 95 cents per dollar of gas tax revenues. Mr. Cornyn won 55%-43% -- a fair reflection of basic party identification in Texas in recent years, according to The National Journal's Almanac of American Politics.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/cornyn_john_per"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Cornyn, John</skos:prefLabel>
  </rdf:Description>
