    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Corzine, Jon S</skos:prefLabel>
    <nyt:associated_article_count rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">436</nyt:associated_article_count>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated Nov. 4, 2009  
Jon S. Corzine, the governor of New Jersey, lost a re-election bid to former prosecutor Christopher J. Christie on Nov. 3, 2009, in one of the year's most closely watched elections.
Mr. Christie overcame a huge Democratic voter advantage and a relentless barrage of negative commercials to defeat Mr. Corzine, an unpopular incumbent who outspent him by more than two to one. Mr. Corzine drew heavily on political help from the White House, including three visits to the state from President Obama.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/c/jon_s_corzine/index.html"/>
