  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/N79716583549066552003">
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">1</nyt:number_of_variants>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2005-01-30</nyt:first_use>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-08-17</nyt:latest_use>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.don_imus"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/imus_don_per"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated Aug. 6, 2009
Don Imus has been saying outrageous things on air ever since he got behind a microphone. It's a trait that has made him one of the nation's most popular radio hosts, but has also regularly landed him in trouble.
Since arriving on the New York scene in 1971, his ups and down since then have included battles with drugs and alcohol, and controversies over comments deemed racist, sexist and homophobic. Then in April 2007, Mr. Imus called the members of the Rutgers women's basketball team, who had made it to the NCAA finals, "nappy-headed ho's.'' After initially suspending him, CBS and NBC, which broadcasts his show over MSNBC, fired him altogether after the controversy continued and major advertisers began deserting the show.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:associated_article_count rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">57</nyt:associated_article_count>
    <nyt:search_api_query rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://api.nytimes.com/svc/search/v1/article?query=+nytd_per_facet%3A%5BImus%2C+Don%5D&amp;rank=newest&amp;fields=abstract,author,body,byline,classifiers_facet,column_facet,date,day_of_week_facet,des_facet,desk_facet,fee,geo_facet,lead_paragraph,material_type_facet,multimedia,nytd_byline,nytd_des_facet,nytd_geo_facet,nytd_lead_paragraph,nytd_org_facet,nytd_per_facet,nytd_section_facet,nytd_title,nytd_works_mentioned_facet,org_facet,page_facet,per_facet,publication_day,publication_month,publication_year,section_page_facet,small_image_height,small_image_url,small_image_width,source_facet,title,url,word_count,works_mentioned_facet</nyt:search_api_query>
