    <nyt:search_api_query rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://api.nytimes.com/svc/search/v1/article?query=+nytd_per_facet%3A%5BRaimi%2C+Sam%5D&amp;rank=newest&amp;fields=abstract,author,body,byline,classifiers_facet,column_facet,date,day_of_week_facet,des_facet,desk_facet,fee,geo_facet,lead_paragraph,material_type_facet,multimedia,nytd_byline,nytd_des_facet,nytd_geo_facet,nytd_lead_paragraph,nytd_org_facet,nytd_per_facet,nytd_section_facet,nytd_title,nytd_works_mentioned_facet,org_facet,page_facet,per_facet,publication_day,publication_month,publication_year,section_page_facet,small_image_height,small_image_url,small_image_width,source_facet,title,url,word_count,works_mentioned_facet</nyt:search_api_query>
    <nyt:associated_article_count rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">11</nyt:associated_article_count>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/r/sam_raimi/index.html"/>
    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2004-11-30</nyt:first_use>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Sam Raimi is best known as the director of the three highly successful ?Spider-Man? movies. He first came to attention with his horror films ?The Evil Dead? (1981) and ?Evil Dead II? (1987).
His other credits include ?Darkman? (1990); ?The Quick and the Dead? (1995), a western with Gene Hackman and Sharon Stone; ?A Simple Plan? (1998), a thriller with Bill Paxton, Bridget Fonda and Billy Bob Thornton; and ?The Gift? (2000), a suspense film starring Cate Blanchett, Keanu Reaves, Katie Holmes and Hilary Swank.
According to thenumbers.com, which tracks business information on movies, the three Spider-Man movies have combined grosses of more than $1.1 billion in the United States and nearly $2.5 billion worldwide.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
