  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/N47525984098330713443">
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Newsom, Gavin</skos:prefLabel>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2004-11-05</nyt:first_use>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/newsom_gavin_per"/>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.gavin_newsom"/>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated July 2, 2009
Gavin Newsom (born 1967) is the popular and telegenic mayor of San Francisco and a Democratic candidate for California governor.
Mr. Newsom, who earned a small fortune as a wine entrepreneur, became the eminence of the gay-marriage movement in 2004 when he authorized same-sex unions in San Francisco. His identification with same-sex marriage should help him among California Democrats, 68 percent of whom opposed Proposition 8. But the issue has also made him a ready lightning rod.
As a candidate and as a mayor, Mr. Newsom is sensitive about being defined by gay marriage and emphasizes his broader portfolio. He speaks constantly about the environment and technology initiatives, which he presents as cornerstones of his leadership approach.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/n/gavin_newsom/index.html"/>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-11-11</nyt:latest_use>
