    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/leno_jay_per"/>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-11-12</nyt:latest_use>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: Sept. 14, 2009
For more than a decade, Jay Leno led the late-night television ratings as a talk show host on "The Tonight Show" on NBC. On Sept. 14, 2009, he began "The Jay Leno Show," Monday through Friday nights at 10 on NBC, no longer competing with David Letterman but with shows like "C.S.I.: Miami." His new program is expected to have little talk, less music and lots more comedy than "The Tonight Show" had featured. He will be a linchpin of NBC's prime-time fortunes.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
