    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2004-09-05</nyt:first_use>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/a/pedro_almodovar/index.html"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Almodovar, Pedro</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: Oct. 29, 2009
Pedro Almodóvar, an award winning director, producer and screenwriter, is arguably the most successful and internationally known Spanish filmmaker of his generation.
Mr. Almodóvar won an Academy Award for "Talk to Her" in 2002 for best original screenplay, and films such as "Women on the Verge of a Nervous Breakdown," "The Flower of My Secret" and "All About My Mother" have earned him numerous accolades and a worldwide following.
Combining complex narratives, shocking irreverence and a wry sense of humor, Mr. Almodóvar's films are nevertheless earnest in their investigations of desire, passion, family and identity and in their nuanced depictions of relationships among women.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">1</nyt:number_of_variants>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-12-07</nyt:latest_use>
