  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/38191738716818567353">
    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2006-04-16</nyt:first_use>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/s/bartlett_sher/index.html"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: April 22, 2009
Bartlett Sher (known as Bart) has emerged in the last few years as one of the most original and exciting directors, not only in the American theater but also in the international world of opera.
In April 2008, his revival at Lincoln Center’s Vivian Beaumont Theater of Rodgers and Hammerstein’s “South Pacific,” the first Broadway revival since the original production closed in 1954, won almost universal critical praise. Ben Brantley in The New York Times called it “rapturous.” Mr. Sher won the Tony for best director that year.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <nyt:associated_article_count rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">19</nyt:associated_article_count>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Sher, Bartlett</skos:prefLabel>
