    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">1</nyt:number_of_variants>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2008-07-21</nyt:latest_use>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Heidi Fleiss became known as the ?Hollywood Madame? after being charged with running an exclusive call-girl ring that catered to the entertainment industry in 1993. She was convicted in 1995 on eight counts of conspiracy, income-tax evasion and money laundering and sentenced in January 1997 to 37 months in Federal prison.
Prosecutors said she had laundered at least $300,000 in income from her sex business through her family's bank accounts and a $1.6 million Beverly Hills estate.
Models-turned-prostitutes had recounted being sent around the globe to service Ms. Fleiss's clients, sometimes earning $10,000 for a single assignment.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Fleiss, Heidi</skos:prefLabel>
