    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Gettelfinger, Ron</skos:prefLabel>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-12-17</nyt:latest_use>
    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2005-06-23</nyt:first_use>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/gettelfinger_ron_per"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated April 1, 2009
Ron Gettelfinger is the president of the United Auto Workers, a post that has put him at the center of the debate over the fate of the Big Three car companies as G.M. and Chrysler are under pressure to make major changes to avoid bankruptcy.
Mr. Gettelfinger has spent his entire career in the car business; his first job was at Ford's truck plant in Louisville, Ky.
In public, his bearing can be reserved, although he is affectionate with his fellow union members, exchanging warm handshakes and manly hugs and greeting members as "brother" or "sister" in the union movement's tradition.</skos:definition>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.ron_gettelfinger"/>
  </rdf:Description>
