  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/29105143839735665623">
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">McClellan, Scott</skos:prefLabel>
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">2</nyt:number_of_variants>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Scott McClellan served as President Bush?s press secretary from 2003 to 2006. Mr. McClellan started working for Mr. Bush when he was the governor of Texas, and came to the White House in 2001 as part of the group of Texans who formed a tight-knit circle around the President.
As press secretary, Mr. McClellan won few points for flair, but presented a steadfast defense of the administration as its problems deepened. He was pushed out of the job in April 2006 as part of a White House staff shakeup, and replaced by Tony Snow, a television commentator.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:associated_article_count rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">28</nyt:associated_article_count>
