    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2004-09-12</nyt:first_use>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: April 6, 2009
Johan Santana is a left-handed pitcher for the New York Mets, and is the cornerstone of the team's rotation. The Mets aquired Santana from the Minnesota Twins in 2008 in a six-year, $137.5 million deal. But his first season with the Mets was tumulutous as he had to adjust to the pressures of playing in New York and to the chaotic first few months, in which his manager and two coaches lost their jobs.
He was booed in his home debut for giving up three home runs in a Mets loss, became frustrated during a stretch when he received little run support and went nearly six weeks between victories.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:associated_article_count rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">104</nyt:associated_article_count>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-12-14</nyt:latest_use>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/s/johan_santana/index.html"/>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Santana, Johan</skos:prefLabel>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/santana_johan_per"/>
  </rdf:Description>
