    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Snyder, Leslie Crocker</skos:prefLabel>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/snyder_leslie_crocker_per"/>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.leslie_crocker_snyder"/>
    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2005-01-13</nyt:first_use>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated Sept. 16, 2009
, Mr. Morgenthau's hand-picked successor. Cyrus R. Vance Jr. Leslie Crocker Snyder, a former prosecutor and judge, has run two unsuccessful campaigns to become Manhattan District Attorney. Ms. Snyder ran against the incument district attorney, Robert M. Morgenthau, in the 2005 DEmocratic primary. In 2009 she lost to
Ms. Snyder was a prosecutor in Manhattan for nine years, during which time she founded and led the sex crimes prosecution bureau. She had a brief stint as a criminal defense lawyer, and became a judge in 1983 in Manhattan Criminal Court. She was appointed to the New York State Supreme Court in 1986 and remained on the bench until 2003, earning a reputation for being tough on crime. She is now a partner at Kasowitz, Benson, Torres &amp; Friedman.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:associated_article_count rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">24</nyt:associated_article_count>
