    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated July 6, 2009
Andy Roddick is a Grand Slam tennis champion who won the U.S. Open in 2003 and finished that season as the world’s number one player, at age 21. His third championship match at Wimbledon in 2009 fell short when he lost a fifth set to Roger Federer by a score of 16-14, the longest deciding set in Grand Slam history.
Roddick held serve for all 37 games in the four-hour-18-minute match before Federer finally broke his serve and won.
If not for Roger Federer, Roddick might have five Grand Slam titles. He lost to Federer in the final match at Wimbledon in 2004 and 2005, and at the U.S. Open in 2006.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Roddick, Andy</skos:prefLabel>
