    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: July 20, 2009
, he sharply criticized the government's handling of the post-election unrest, saying it had lost the trust of many Iranians, and called for the release of hundreds of those arrested in recent weeks. speech at Friday prayers on July 18 . In the turmoil that followed the disputed vote, Mr. Rafsanjani himself stayed silent for over a month and was said he was working behind the scenes to forge a compromise. But in a  President Mahmoud Ahmadinejad  against  Mir Hussein Moussavi  from 1989 to 1997 and is one of the nation's richest and most powerful men. During the 2009 presidential campaign, he supported  Iran Ali Akbar Hashemi Rafsanjani was president of</skos:definition>
