  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/67702730710450123773">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The National Journal's Almanac of American Politics 2008: Adapted from
Saxby Chambliss (R-GA), the senior senator from Georgia, was elected in 2002 after serving four terms in the House. He was re-elected in a 2008 runoff election against Democratic challenger Jim Martin. Chambliss grew up in Shreveport, Louisiana, the son of an Episcopalian minister.
Chambliss challenged Democratic Senator Max Cleland in 2002. Cleland had a compelling biography. After college he volunteered for the Army and went to Vietnam in 1967; he lost both legs and his right arm when a loose grenade exploded.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/c/saxby_chambliss/index.html"/>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/chambliss_saxby_per"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Chambliss, Saxby</skos:prefLabel>
