    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: April 24, 2009
for accepting improper gifts from a contributor. admonished by the Senate Ethics Committee Robert G. Torricelli is a lobbyist and a former United States senator from New Jersey. He was one of the Senate's most flamboyant personalities and prodigious fund-raisers until he abruptly quit the 2002 race after being
's widening pension corruption investigation. Andrew M. Cuomo In April 2009 Mr. Torricelli's name was added to the list of people linked to Attorney General
on fraud charges, as was David Loglisci, the top investment officer of the state pension fund. indicted in March , was  Alan G. Hevesi , a spokesman for Mr. Torricelli confirmed on April 23, 2009. Mr. Morris, who was once the chief political adviser to New York's former state comptroller  Hank Morris From 2005 to 2008, Mr. Torricelli did work for Searle &amp; Company, a Connecticut investment firm that employed his longtime friend</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Torricelli, Robert G</skos:prefLabel>
