    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: July 7, 2009
's ''Tonight Show." NBC Conan O'Brien is a comedian, television writer and talk show host known for a self-deprecating persona that is equal parts silly and quick-witted. On June 1, 2009, Mr. O'Brien replaced Jay Leno as host of
Although he affects his own version of the glibly ironic stance that has been a standard for late-night hosts since David Letterman, Mr. O'Brien has always given the impression that deep down inside he's a sweet guy who just wants to be liked. It was the quality that kept a cluster of loyal viewers tuning in until he found both a unique comedic voice and a sizable audience for "Late Night with Conan O'Brien," which ran for 16 years.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-11-12</nyt:latest_use>
