    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2007-06-15</nyt:first_use>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Waldheim, Kurt</skos:prefLabel>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.kurt_waldheim"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Kurt Waldheim served two terms as Secretary-General of the United Nations and was elected president of Austria in 1986. But Mr. Waldheim's diplomatic career was overshadowed by revelations about his hidden Nazi past that first appeared during his campaign for the presidency.
A committee of international historians appointed by the Austrian government concluded that Mr. Waldheim had served in units that had been involved in slaughtering civilians in Yugoslavia and sending Greek Jews to death camps, and that Mr. Waldheim had been present when some of these acts were planned, if not when they were carried out.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
