    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated Sept. 30, 2009
. Michael R. Bloomberg  before narrowly losing the 2001 mayoral race to  Rudolph W. Giuliani Mark Green was the first person to hold the office of New York City's public advocate, serving from 1994 to 2001. He famously sparred with
, who later won the general election. After that race, Mr. Green said he would retire from politics and ruled out running again.   Andrew M. Cuomo Mr. Green attempted a political comeback in 2006, running for the Democratic nomination for state attorney general, but was beaten by</skos:definition>
