  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/87494708033537385573">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.kim_clijsters"/>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Clijsters, Kim</skos:prefLabel>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-10-26</nyt:latest_use>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated Sept. 14, 2009
Kim Clijsters was the wild-card 2009 U.S. Open entry from Belgium who captured the title by defeating the 19-year-old Caroline Wozniacki of Denmark, 7-5, 6-3, before an adoring crowd of 23,351 at Arthur Ashe Stadium.
Clijsters, a former No. 1 player, left the game in 2007 to start a family and returned to tennis just months before the 2009 Open.
She was the first unseeded woman to win the United States Open, at least in the Open era, and in the process she became the first mother to win a Grand Slam title since Evonne Goolagong Cawley won Wimbledon in 1980. A crowd favorite, Clijster played with maturity and skill in her comeback in the Open.</skos:definition>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/clijsters_kim_per"/>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/c/kim_clijsters/index.html"/>
