    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: Nov. 23, 2009
for over three years. Sergeant Shalit has been promoted to staff sergeant from corporal during his captivity. Hamas Gilad Shalit, an Israeli soldier, was seized from Israeli territory by Hamas and other Palestinian militant groups in a cross-border raid and was dragged into Gaza, wounded, in June 2006. He has been a hostage of
All attempts to obtain Sergeant Shalit's return, through an exchange for Palestinian prisoners in Israel, have so far failed. He has been allowed no visits by the Red Cross. The last sign that he was alive was a handwritten letter to his parents in June 2008.</skos:definition>
