    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Santa Fe, N.M. Home:    Roman Catholic Religion:    None Children:    Barbara Flavin; married 1972. Spouse:    B.A., Tufts University, 1970; M.A., Tufts' Fletcher School of Law and Diplomacy, 1971 Education:    Pasadena, Calif. Place of Birth:    Nov. 15, 1947 Date of Birth:    Staff, U.S. House of Representatives, 1971-72; Staff, U.S. Department of State, 1973-75; Staff, Senate Foreign Relations Subcommittee, 1975-78; Executive Director, NM Democratic Party, 1978; Executive Director, Bernalillo County Democratic Committee, 1978; President, Richardson Trade Group, 1978-82; U.S. Ambassador to U.N., 1997-98; Secretary, U.S. Department of Energy, 1998-2000; Senior Managing Director, Kissinger McLarty, Washington, 2001-2002 Business/Professional Experience:    Governor of New Mexico; elected 2002; U.S. Representative from NM, 1983-1997 Political Office:    Democratic Party:    William Blaine Richardson III Full Name:</skos:definition>
    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2005-01-15</nyt:first_use>
