  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/88503243022993576703">
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/crist_charlie_per"/>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-12-19</nyt:latest_use>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/c/charlie_crist/index.html"/>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: Nov. 16, 2009
Charlie Crist, the Republican governor of Florida since 2006, is facing an unexpectedly rocky road in his campaign for the United States Senate seat vacated by Senator Mel Martinez. Mr. Crist, a moderate who has enjoyed popularity with many Democrats, now faces a primary challenger and increasingly angry opposition from conservative Republicans.
A raft of conservative groups, commentators and politicians are supporting a primary challenge to Mr. Crist by Marco Rubio, a telegenic former speaker of the Florida House christened a Reaganite's answer to Mr. Obama by The National Review.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">1</nyt:number_of_variants>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Crist, Charlie</skos:prefLabel>
