  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/62944836219330938653">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2004-11-05</nyt:first_use>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: Aug. 7, 2009
The maverick Broadway producer Rocco Landesman is the new chairman of the National Endowment for the Arts, the nation's largest and most important arts organization.
Mr. Landesman was nominated by President Obama in May and confirmed by the Senate on Aug. 7, filling the post vacated by Dana Gioia. He is expected to lobby hard for more financing for the arts. But he is not famous for his skills as an administrator or diplomat. Rather, Mr. Landesman is known for his energy, intellect and irreverent -- and occasionally sharp-elbowed -- candor.</skos:definition>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/landesman_rocco_per"/>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-09-09</nyt:latest_use>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Landesman, Rocco</skos:prefLabel>
