  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/N11359629169670069533">
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.brian_leetch"/>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/l/brian_leetch/index.html"/>
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-11-09</nyt:latest_use>
    <nyt:associated_article_count rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">10</nyt:associated_article_count>
    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2005-09-24</nyt:first_use>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/leetch_brian_per"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated Nov. 10, 2009
Brian Leetch was inducted into the Hockey Hall of Fame on Nov. 9, 2009. He was celebrated for his many achievements as a Rangers defenseman and as a keystone player on what may have been the best United States national team ever assembled.
Leetch played for 18 N.H.L. seasons, 16 ½ of them with the Rangers. He scored 247 goals and had 1,028 points in 1,205 regular-season games, and added 28 goals and 97 points in 95 playoff games.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">1</nyt:number_of_variants>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
