    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: Nov. 24, 2009
). He is currently serving time in an Israeli prison. Hamas  political parties (the other is  Palestinian , the larger of the two main  Fatah Marwan Barghouti is a popular leader of
Mr. Barghouti, a West Bank farmer's son who joined Yasser Arafat's Fatah group when he was 15, was among those who worked with Mr. Arafat on reaching the 1993 Oslo accords, which established Palestinian authority in the territories occupied by Israel in 1967. He was seized by Israeli troops in April 2002, and accused of being one of the principal organizers behind the wave of armed attacks and suicide bombings aimed at Israelis.</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Barghouti, Marwan</skos:prefLabel>
  </rdf:Description>
