  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/66006368834048343263">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: May 26, 2009
Mr. Patrick was a strong supporter of Barack Obama in 2008 -- the two were close enough that Mr. Obama borrowed a line from a speech by Mr. Deval, which led to charges of plagiarism -- and Mr. Deval's name quickly appeared on short lists of potential Supreme Court nominees when word spread that Justice David H. Souter intended to retire. President Obama eventually selected Sonia Sotomayor. Deval Laurdine Patrick made the trip from the streets of Chicago to the office of the governor of Massachusetts, the first black to hold the position.</skos:definition>
