  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/N55307210480758257143">
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2008-04-01</nyt:latest_use>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/g/christine_o_gregoire/index.html"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/gregoire_christine_o_per"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: May 26, 2009
Christine O. Gregoire is the governor of Washington. Ms. Gregoire, a Democrat, was narrowly elected in 2004 in one of the closest gubernatorial contests in American history, winning by 133 votes. She was decisively reelected in 2008.
As governor, Ms. Gregoire has signed a measure making Washington the second state, after California, to grant paid leave to workers after the birth of a child. She has also signed bills expanding gay rights and championed education and gambling reforms.
As state attorney general, Ms. Gregoire was one of the chief negotiators who forged an agreement in 1998 between tobacco companies and 46 states that resulted in a $206 billion settlement.</skos:definition>
