    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated July 20, 2009
Stewart Cink is a professional golfer from Huntsville, Alabama. In July 2009, he won his first major golf tournament, the British Open.
Cink defeated Tom Watson in a four-hole playoff at Turnberry, after making a 15-foot birdie putt on the 18th hole. Cink has won six times on the Professional Golf Association (PGA) tour. He has been a member of four United States Ryder Cup teams, and was rookie of the year on the PGA tour in 1997. The previous season, he was named player of the year on the Nationwide Tour. Cink played college golf at Georgia Tech where he was a three-time All-American.</skos:definition>
