    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated July 9, 2009
, in December 2007. Nestor Kirchner Cristina Fernández de Kirchner is the first woman to be elected president in Argentina’s history. She succeeded her husband,
In 2009, Mr. Kirchner ran for the lower house of Congress in a bid to resuscitate the flagging administration of Mrs. Kirchner, who has struggled to muster more than a 30 percent approval in opinion polls. Mr. Kirchner is a combative and often stubborn politician who is widely viewed to be deeply involved in running the government led by his wife.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
