  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/89479892985862227453">
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.john_allen_muhammad"/>
    <nyt:number_of_variants rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">8</nyt:number_of_variants>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: Nov. 10, 2009
John A. Muhammad was the sniper who directed a string of random killings that terrified the Washington region in 2002. The mysterious shootings, which began on Oct. 2, 2002, left 10 people dead and wounded 3. Mr. Muhammad, 48, was executed by lethal injection on Nov. 10, 2009, a day after the Supreme Court turned down his appeal.
Mr. Muhammad was sentenced to death in 2003 for two counts of capital murder in the killing of Dean H. Meyers, 53, in Manassas, Va. One count was under a newly enacted state antiterrorism law; the second was for committing multiple murders in three years. Mr. Muhammad was also sentenced to 10 years for conspiracy to commit murder and 3 on a gun charge. Mr. Muhammad carried out the shootings with Lee Boyd Malvo, who was also found guilty of murder. Mr. Malvo, also known as John Lee Malvo, was sentenced to life in prison without parole.</skos:definition>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
