    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.akihito"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: June 25, 2009
. The Japanese government named his era of rule Heisei, or Achieving Peace. November 12, 1990 . He was formally enthroned on  Emperor Hirohito  on January 7, 1989 after the death of his father  Chrysanthemum Throne Emperor Akihito is the 125th emperor of Japan. He acceded to the
Emperor Akihito was born in Tokyo on Dec. 23, 1933, after his parents had a succession of four girls. His dynasty has presided over the the oldest hereditary monarchy in the world since the earliest years of recorded Japanese history, at least 1,300 years ago.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
