    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated July 20, 2009
.  Mahmoud Ahmadinejad  from 1997 to 2005. A moderate by Iranian terms, he struggled with the country's hard-line clerics to bring more openness to the economy and for better relations with the West. In recent years he has criticized the political and economic performance of the current president,  Iran Mohammad Khatami was president of
. Mir Hussein Moussavi Mr. Khatami's supporters pressed him to run in the June 2009 presidential elections, and on Feb. 8,  he  announced that he would run. But in March, the charismatic reformist cleric withdrew from the race to support a political ally and former prime minister,</skos:definition>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Khatami, Mohammad</skos:prefLabel>
    <nyt:search_api_query rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">http://api.nytimes.com/svc/search/v1/article?query=+nytd_per_facet%3A%5BKhatami%2C+Mohammad%5D&amp;rank=newest&amp;fields=abstract,author,body,byline,classifiers_facet,column_facet,date,day_of_week_facet,des_facet,desk_facet,fee,geo_facet,lead_paragraph,material_type_facet,multimedia,nytd_byline,nytd_des_facet,nytd_geo_facet,nytd_lead_paragraph,nytd_org_facet,nytd_per_facet,nytd_section_facet,nytd_title,nytd_works_mentioned_facet,org_facet,page_facet,per_facet,publication_day,publication_month,publication_year,section_page_facet,small_image_height,small_image_url,small_image_width,source_facet,title,url,word_count,works_mentioned_facet</nyt:search_api_query>
