  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/47223551956333338213">
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2006-08-05</nyt:first_use>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The English composer Thomas AdÃ¨s, born March 1, 1971, achieved prominence at an early age for his viscerally appealing and intellectually stimulating music. Major orchestral works include "Asyla" (1997), which won the prestigious Grawemeyer Award in 2000, and "Tevot" (2007). Both were given their premieres by Simon Rattle, a champion of Mr. AdÃ¨s. His catalog also includes two operas: "The Tempest" (2004) and "Powder Her Face" (1995), a piano quintet and string quartet, a violin concerto, pieces for piano solo and many chamber works.
Trademarks of Mr. AdÃ¨s's music, written in a distinctive voice, include unusually high sonorities, innovative percussion and rhythmic vigor. Unlike many living composers, he has not used electronic elements.</skos:definition>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.thomas_ades"/>
