    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated Aug. 19, 2009
By Rachel Donadio
. Metropolitan Opera , from his flower-child-era film of "Romeo and Juliet" (1968) to his opulent productions at the  Franco Zeffirelli Few Italians since Federico Fellini have had such an impact in the United States as
accessible, while his productions of "La Bohème," "La Traviata" and other Italian operas have kept audiences coming to the Met, which in 2008 honored him with a gala. Shakespeare  -- have helped make  Mel Gibson , and "Hamlet" (1990), starring  Richard Burton  and  Elizabeth Taylor For decades, his films -- including "The Taming of the Shrew" (1967), with</skos:definition>
