  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/N49137835183882196443">
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Michael Chertoff, the former secretary of homeland security, came to th job with experience in fighting terrorism, having served as the head of the Justice Department's criminal division in the months after Sept. 11th.
He began his prosecutorial career working in Manhattan under Rudolph W. Giuliani, and was named United States Attorney in New Jersey by President George H.W. Bush, a post in which he made a reputation by pursuing political corruption cases. His introduction to Washington came as counsel for Republicans on the Senate Whitewater Committee. In 2003, after Mr. Chertoff had proved instrumental in winning approval of the Patriot Act and other anti-terrorism measures, President Bush appointed him as an appeals court judge.</skos:definition>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.michael_chertoff"/>
