    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Tymoshenko, Yulia V</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: June 23, 2009
Yulia V. Tymoshenko is the prime minister of the Ukraine. A hero of the country's so-called Orange Revolution, which peacefully ousted a pro-Russian regime in 2005, Ms. Tymoshenko has been at the center of a deepening political paralysis that has crushed many of the high hopes that greeted the establishment of a pro-Western government.
In the last weeks of 2004, as a crisis over the outcome of the presidential election deepened, Ms. Tymoshenko emerged in the Western media as the belligerently populist leader. Her good looks, energy and anti-establishment rhetoric made her an icon of the demonstrations that incapacitated Kiev and resulted in the overturning of a fraudulent presidential election.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
