    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.bill_deblasio"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated Nov. 3, 2009
Bill de Blasio, a councilman from Brooklyn, was elected public advocate in 2009, easily defeating his Republican opponent, Alex T. Zablocki.
The public advocate is the city's ombudsman and second-highest elected official, responsible for monitoring and reviewing city agencies, and is next in line to succeed the mayor if he is unable to serve.
Mr. de Blasio's victory could quickly make him a strong contender for mayor in 2013.
, who kept a low profile. Betsy Gotbaum 's successful effort to persuade the City Council to amend the term limits law so he could run for a third term. He will certainly be a more outspoken and visible public advocate than the one he would replace,  Michael R. Bloomberg Mr. de Blasio was a vocal critic of Mayor</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/N39038994086498832393">
