  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/N29599226407083600653">
    <nyt:latest_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2009-08-19</nyt:latest_use>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">There is no one quite like Daniel Barenboim today in the music world. General music director of the Berlin State Opera and its orchestra, the Berlin Staatskapelle; principal guest conductor at the Teatro Alla Scala in Milan; formerly music director of the Chicago Symphony and the Orchestre de Paris; for years a conductor at the Bayreuth and Salzburg festivals; a champion of new music since the 1950s; a chamber musician who has performed with every great singer and instrumentalist in half a century, from Gregor Piatigorsky and Dietrich Fischer-Dieskau to his late wife, the cellist Jacqueline du PrÃ©, and the bass-baritone Thomas Quasthoff, Mr. Barenboim was a child prodigy who remains, despite a full-time conducting career, a towering figure at the keyboard.</skos:definition>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.daniel_barenboim"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Barenboim, Daniel</skos:prefLabel>
