    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/d/joseph_v_doria_jr/index.html"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated July 23, 2009
Joseph V. Doria Jr. is commissioner of the New Jersey Department of Community Affairs. He is the former mayor of Bayonne, and has also served in the State Assembly and the State Senate.
F.B.I. Mr. Doria's home was raided on July 23, 2009, part of a sweep in which the mayors of Hoboken and Secaucus, two state assemblymen, five rabbis and dozens of others were rounded up across New Jersey and Brooklyn after a two-year corruption and international money-laundering investigation by the</skos:definition>
