    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: March 27, 2009
By Richard Sandomir
has faded from view as the principal owner, Levine has emerged as the strongest voice of the Yankees, baseball's wealthiest team. He is their executive-as-prosecutor, a tough, short-tempered and smart protector of the Steinbrenner family and the Yankees brand. George Steinbrenner . In recent years, as  Yankees Randy Levine is the president of the
, as labor commissioner and a deputy mayor; and to Steinbrenner, as a personal lawyer and, since 2000, as the team's president. Rudolph W. Giuliani Levine's career has been a succession of increasingly public apprenticeships: to Arnold I. Burns, the deputy attorney general in the Reagan Justice Department; to Mayor</skos:definition>
    <nyt:topicPage rdf:resource="http://topics.nytimes.com/top/reference/timestopics/people/l/randy_l_levine/index.html"/>
