  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://data.nytimes.com/N60626536011216821613">
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Shaul Mofaz is the Israeli Transportation Minister and member of the Kadima party. He is an Iranian-born former army chief of staff and defense minister, a position he was appointed to by then prime minister Ariel Sharon in 2002.
Born in Iran, Mr. Mofaz immigrated to Israel at age 9. After high school, he volunteered for the paratroopers and served during the 1967 Arab-Israeli war, before he began climbing through a series of command positions.
He was an infantry brigade commander in 1982 when Mr. Sharon, then defense minister, ordered Israeli forces to invade Lebanon in pursuit of Mr. Arafat and the Palestine Liberation Organization. He served in that war.</skos:definition>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/mofaz_shaul_per"/>
