    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.carol_m_browner"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">and the other members of his environmental team. Barack Obama , environmental regulation, energy conservation and new technology are very much in line with the views of President  climate change Carol M. Browner, who ran the Environmental Protection Agency under Bill Clinton, is the White House coordinator of energy and climate policy for the Obama administration, a new position. It is unknown how much authority Ms. Browner will wield in this position, but her views on
Along with her record as E.P.A. director, she has a strong résumé in environmental protection, law and management consulting, and a clear determination to break from the Bush record, which she has called “the worst environmental administration ever.” She also sits on the board of the Audubon Society, the League of Conservation Voters and the Alliance for Climate Protection, which advocates control of greenhouse gases.</skos:definition>
    <nyt:associated_article_count rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#int">7</nyt:associated_article_count>
  </rdf:Description>
