    <nyt:first_use rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2004-11-14</nyt:first_use>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: Dec. 14, 2009
, who is retiring in December 2009. Charles Gibson , who is taking over the evening news from  Diane Sawyer George Stephanopoulos is the host on ABC's "Good Morning America." He replaces
. He will continue to host "This Week With George Stephanopoulos" until a successor is named. Bill Clinton Mr. Stephanopoulos went to ABC News after working as a campaign operative and White House adviser for policy and strategy to President
Working next to the Oval Office, Mr. Stephanopoulos kept notoriously grueling hours, dragging himself out of bed at 5 A.M. and often not leaving the White House until 9 P.M. His closeness to the president gave him an extraordinary ability to read Mr. Clinton's mind, and sometimes to lead it, but he also bore the brunt of his boss's occasionally volcanic temper. In 1996, at 35 he left for a new career as a multimillion-dollar author, professor and television talking head.</skos:definition>
  </rdf:Description>
