    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Fischer, Bobby</skos:prefLabel>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Bobby Fischer 1943 - 2008
Bobby Fischer, the iconoclastic genius who was one of the greatest chess players the world has ever seen, died on Jan. 17, 2008 in a hospital in ReykjavÃ­k, Iceland. He was 64.
Mr. Fischer, the most powerful American player in history, had moved to Iceland in 2005. He had emerged briefly in 1992 from a mysterious seclusion that had lasted two decades and defied an American ban on conducting business in war-torn Yugoslavia to play a $5 million match against his old nemesis, the Russian-born grandmaster Boris Spassky.</skos:definition>
    <owl:sameAs rdf:resource="http://rdf.freebase.com/ns/en.bobby_fischer"/>
  </rdf:Description>
