    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Updated: April 16, 2009
Felipe Calderón was elected president of Mexico in 2006. 
laws to make it easier for Mexican immigrants to gain citizenship or temporary work visas, disappointing the Calderón administration. immigration Shortly after his election, Mr. Calderón criticized the United States government for its crackdown on illegal immigrants, saying it has led to the persecution of immigrant workers without visas.  In 2006, the Bush administration stepped up raids on factories and farms suspected of hiring illegal workers, imposing heavy fines and deporting a record number of illegal immigrants. The United States Congress in 2007 failed to approve proposed legislation to revamp</skos:definition>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.nytimes.com/elements/nytd_per"/>
