. It said he had "managed a network of training camps" and had been "involved in every major terrorist operation carried out by Al Qaeda." Osama bin Laden The memo summarized the C.I.A.'s judgment that Abu Zubaydah, then 31, had risen rapidly to "third or fourth man in Al Qaeda" and had served as "senior lieutenant" to</skos:definition>
